1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,266
CURRENT LOCATIONS

2
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,768
SEONGPANAK TEAM
HAS 5.5 KM LEFT UNTIL BAENGNOKDAM

3
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:22,939
9:10 A.M.
SEONGPANAK TEAM LEAVES SOKBAT SHELTER

4
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,858
Goodness.

5
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:26,943
We're still on level ground here, right?

6
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:27,986
I think so.

7
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:30,613
THEY'RE STILL ON THE EASY SECTION

8
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:38,997
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WHILE,
THEY FOCUS QUIETLY ON HIKING

9
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,250
Why are some people coming down?

10
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,252
They probably started early.

11
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:46,421
-They already visited the top?
-Yes.

12
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,257
WE'RE DESCENDING

13
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,385
Some people just go halfway up
to Sara Oreum Volcanic Cone.

14
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:53,678
Is that so?

15
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,805
THE HIKER WITH GOGGLES
SUDDENLY PROVIDES INFORMATION

16
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,307
I guess some just go halfway.

17
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,063
SARA OREUM
A VOLCANIC CONE NEAR SEONGPANAK TRAIL

18
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,898
IT HAS A LAKE FORMED IN ITS SUMMIT CRATER

19
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:11,863
BAENGNOKDAM

20
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,866
Sir, may I ask why you hike?

21
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:15,784
CAR QUIZ?

22
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,368
Us? For health.

23
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:18,703
For health?

24
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:19,829
To stay healthy.

25
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:23,500
And as you get older,
you have to work out your lower body more.

26
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,085
I SEE

27
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,378
In a way,
that's the most practical reason, right?

28
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,421
Right.

29
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:32,383
As someone once said on TV,
when one rises in position…

30
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,637
you tend to hear those under you less.

31
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,431
And when I climb mountains,
I can't hear the sounds from below.

32
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:40,558
You can't hear those below you
when you go up,

33
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,726
so that's why you like it?

34
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:42,811
No, that's not it.

35
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:46,523
THE RELATION BETWEEN HIKING AND LIFE

36
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:49,400
EXPLAINING WHAT IT MEANS
TO CLIMB TO THE TOP

37
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:52,612
I'm sorry,

38
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:54,656
but you're not listening
after asking questions.

39
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:56,032
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

40
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,283
Mr. Car, you only asked and…

41
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,785
GOT CAUGHT TUNING THEM OUT

42
00:01:58,868 --> 00:01:59,702
I was listening.

43
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,538
I was listening to everything he said.

44
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:02,455
You were listening?

45
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:04,290
I was so deeply impressed by his words

46
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:05,959
that I was repeating them in my head.

47
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:08,711
"The higher you go,
the harder it is to hear those below."

48
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:10,672
He said that wasn't it.

49
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:11,589
Sorry?

50
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,007
He just said that wasn't it.

51
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,300
Your lower body must be fit--

52
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,635
That was from way before.

53
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,596
What about you? Are you enjoying it?

54
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:20,598
Are you enjoying hiking?

55
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:22,433
What kind of question is that?

56
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,435
You and I are making the same expression.

57
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:27,021
I'm sorry, but I'm sure
she likes hiking with her dad.

58
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,773
I mean, it's nice to come with your dad.

59
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:30,733
But I want to ask her why she hikes.

60
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:32,235
You don't really know yet, do you?

61
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:35,238
It's not my hobby, so I don't really know.

62
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:36,281
Right?

63
00:02:37,115 --> 00:02:37,991
A SATISFACTORY ANSWER

64
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:39,492
She was making the same face as me.

65
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,911
For those who come with their parents…

66
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,289
when we ask why they hike,

67
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:47,333
they all say
their mom or dad made them go.

68
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,835
Because my mom made me go.

69
00:02:50,753 --> 00:02:52,005
That's hilarious.

70
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:54,716
They were dragged there by their parents.

71
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,594
But I think they're really good children.

72
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:59,512
They're really nice kids.

73
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:01,848
If I was their age
and they made me go hiking…

74
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:05,059
I would've never gone.

75
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:09,022
WHY ON EARTH DO YOU HIKE?
FOR HEALTH AND PARENTS

76
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:12,233
Honestly, I didn't think
I'd be saying this today…

77
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,152
but it's a bit okay.

78
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:16,654
-Up to this point.
-So far.

79
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,406
Up to this point,

80
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:20,491
it even feels like it's pretty good.

81
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,702
-Really?
-We are still on the easy section.

82
00:03:22,785 --> 00:03:24,996
Can't you just not say stuff like that?

83
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:29,834
9:25 A.M.
THEY PASS THE 4.75 KM MARK

84
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:30,877
I feel it now.

85
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:34,881
Now, as the path gets narrower.

86
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,719
The sign.

87
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:41,846
Look at the sign.

88
00:03:42,555 --> 00:03:43,806
GOING FROM EASY TO MODERATE NOW

89
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:44,724
CURRENT LOCATION

90
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:47,602
THEY MUST HIKE THE MODERATE SECTION
FOR 1 HOUR AND 20 MINUTES

91
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:50,230
As long as the path doesn't turn rocky,
it should be fine.

92
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,189
Exactly.

93
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:53,483
It doesn't feel like it will though.

94
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:54,400
Right.

95
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:56,569
There might be some stairs.

96
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:57,487
Right.

97
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:04,786
CONFIDENTLY MOVING THROUGH
THE MODERATE SECTION

98
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:06,287
Someone wrote "Car, the garden."

99
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:08,665
What's this?

100
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:11,584
CAR, THE GARDEN

101
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:12,669
Yeah, that's me.

102
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,671
It's me, everyone.

103
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:19,259
SLOWLY STARTING TO SWEAT

104
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:21,469
Are we actually getting better?

105
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:24,013
Our standards
must've been raised too high.

106
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:27,725
Seoraksan was…

107
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:29,686
Damn…

108
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:30,895
Well, I shouldn't say that.

109
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:34,107
Seoraksan was definitely a tough mountain.

110
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,692
Hallasan is doable.

111
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:37,944
If you come to Jeju Island,

112
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:41,656
it's worth climbing once.

113
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:43,658
Okay, this is so nice.

114
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:45,535
You can do it.

115
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:48,204
What's this?

116
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,623
HIKERS WITHOUT SHIRTS ON
RUNNING DOWN THE MOUNTAIN

117
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,041
Gosh, so young and cool.

118
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:52,959
You can do it.

119
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:54,377
It's Car, the garden! Hello.

120
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,795
-You can do it.
-That's amazing.

121
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,171
That's so cool.

122
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:58,965
Look at them.

123
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:00,967
I love you!

124
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:02,135
-I love you too.
-Very cool.

125
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:03,219
Good luck.

126
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,346
They're so cool.

127
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,556
They're so passionate.

128
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:10,518
<i>I've received passionate support</i>
<i>from men in their twenties.</i>

129
00:05:10,601 --> 00:05:12,312
They go crazy for me.

130
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:16,607
I think I get
a lot of love and support from men.

131
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,067
But I'm not sure if it's love…

132
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:21,446
or if they just want to mess with me.

133
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:23,740
But it's fine either way.

134
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:27,744
MEANWHILE, THE GWANEUMSA TEAM

135
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:32,540
WALKING THROUGH THE HARD SECTION

136
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:44,510
THE UPHILL CLIMB NEVER ENDS

137
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:48,973
Geez.

138
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:51,392
This is tough.

139
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,896
I really wanted to quit the show.

140
00:05:57,607 --> 00:06:00,568
THE PATH KEEPS GETTING STEEPER

141
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:04,614
AND THEY KEEP BENDING LOWER

142
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,576
AS THEY KEEP CLIMBING WITHOUT REST

143
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:12,663
SMILES DISAPPEAR FROM THEIR FACES

144
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,583
GRUNTS

145
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:16,793
Damn it.

146
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:22,757
ON THE MERCILESS INCLINE

147
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:29,305
THEIR STAMINA RUNS OUT

148
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,808
Let's rest up there.

149
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:34,185
It's hot.

150
00:06:34,268 --> 00:06:36,938
9:30 A.M.
THEY TAKE A SHORT BREAK

151
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:40,274
BOTH HUNCHED OVER

152
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:46,030
DOWOON TAKES OFF
HIS LIGHTWEIGHT PADDED JACKET

153
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:47,990
Geez.

154
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:50,326
Gosh.

155
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,369
Goodness.

156
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,248
YOON DORAEMON'S BAG IS FULL

157
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:56,499
Give me some of the food.

158
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:57,708
I'll put it in my bag.

159
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,877
The food is at the very bottom. It's okay.

160
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,212
Can you put this inside then?

161
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:02,338
-Okay.
-Thanks.

162
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,256
Here.

163
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:04,924
INTO TARZZAN'S BAG

164
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:05,925
It fits perfectly.

165
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:06,968
Thanks.

166
00:07:08,427 --> 00:07:10,012
LAST-MINUTE REFUELING WITH SNACKS

167
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,305
-Clif bar?
-Yes.

168
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:15,226
9:40 A.M.
SETTING OFF AGAIN AFTER A SHORT BREAK

169
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:16,853
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

170
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:18,271
Dowoon, you go first.

171
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:21,607
You go first. I'm a bit slow.

172
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:24,235
CURRENT LOCATION
GAEMIDEUNG RIDGE

173
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:26,529
WHAT'S LEFT NOW IS THE SECOND CRUX

174
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:30,074
DRONE FILMING WAS ALLOWED AFTER DISCUSSION
WITH HALLASAN NATIONAL PARK

175
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,325
GAEMIDEUNG

176
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:35,830
THE AREA WHERE THE RIDGE IS SHAPED
LIKE AN ANT'S BACK

177
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:39,417
A STEEP INCLINE

178
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:43,045
A LONG RIDGE

179
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:49,594
ONCE THEY PASS THE RIDGE,
THEY'LL ARRIVE AT THE SAMGAKBONG SHELTER

180
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:53,097
THEY ENTER
WHERE GAEMIDEUNG'S INCLINE STARTS

181
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,142
This is pretty intense.

182
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:57,185
Damn it.

183
00:07:58,769 --> 00:08:01,689
WITH A TOUGH INCLINE

184
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,735
THEY KEEP THEIR EYES DOWN
AND MARCH AHEAD

185
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:18,456
<i>I found Gaemideung so annoying.</i>

186
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,546
Gosh, Dowoon.

187
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:33,471
DEEP EXHALE

188
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:35,681
My calves are about to burst.

189
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:43,940
WHAT WERE YOU THINKING
WHEN YOU WALKED THROUGH GAEMIDEUNG?

190
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:45,942
I thought…

191
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:48,611
"Why did I agree to do this?"

192
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,741
<i>The ridge just wouldn't end.</i>

193
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:56,536
<i>No matter how much we walked,</i>
<i>we were still on it.</i>

194
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:02,583
I thought, "Ants are supposed to be small.
Why is it so big?"

195
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,835
"They named it so strangely."

196
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,714
Man, I really miss…

197
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:11,133
going downhill.

198
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:17,431
HE HAS NO ENERGY TO REPLY

199
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:19,475
How much is left until the shelter?

200
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:20,560
No, don't think about it.

201
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:22,937
-Thinking is a luxury.
-I'm hungry.

202
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:26,148
I can't wait to eat.

203
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:33,072
THE MERCILESS RIDGE
TEASES AN END THAT DOESN'T COME

204
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:38,327
MEANWHILE, THE SEONGPANAK TEAM
IS PASSING THE MODERATE SECTION

205
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,787
I'm starting to feel it now.

206
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,747
Gosh.

207
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:45,001
EXCLAIMING

208
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,753
PRODUCER NAH AND CAR, THE GARDEN
ARE STARTING TO STRUGGLE

209
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:51,048
You can raise your hand
whenever you want to rest.

210
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,967
Okay.

211
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:55,344
Can we rest at the next area with benches?

212
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:56,762
-Sure.
-Okay.

213
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,306
IT WAS NAH WHO WANTED TO REST

214
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:03,060
I see a sort of deck area there.

215
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,437
Good, a deck sounds nice.

216
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,813
Shall we sit down for a bit?

217
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:08,649
THEY FIND A SHELTER ON THE HILL

218
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,777
It's so steep here.

219
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:13,946
It feels a bit like Seoraksan here.

220
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,073
This is pretty tough.

221
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,410
AFTER THE INCLINE,
THEY ARRIVE AT THE SHELTER

222
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,289
Should I give the other guys a call?

223
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,710
-Will they pick up?
-I don't think they have a signal.

224
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:31,088
I wondered if they were surviving
and if they were climbing all right.

225
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,424
I called to check on them,
but I couldn't reach them.

226
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,301
I thought,
"They must be having a hard time."

227
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:41,098
THEY ARE HAVING A VERY HARD TIME

228
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:42,433
<i>If we go 1.2 km more…</i>

229
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:44,810
1.2 KM AWAY FROM THE JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

230
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:47,855
Since it's 1.2 km,
it should take about an hour, right?

231
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:49,732
Then, wouldn't we make it in 40 minutes?

232
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:51,525
Who do you mean by "we?"

233
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,194
If it weren't for you, we could go now.

234
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,737
HIKERS HAVE HAD HEART ATTACKS HERE

235
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,447
DON'T OVERDO IT AND TAKE IT SLOW

236
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:57,531
PRODUCER NAH IS SHOCKED

237
00:10:57,615 --> 00:11:00,785
9:58 A.M.
THEY SET OFF AGAIN

238
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:12,880
HOLDING ONTO THE ROPE FOR THE TOUGH PATH

239
00:11:14,548 --> 00:11:16,092
SIGHING

240
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,051
EXCLAIMING

241
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:28,938
<i>I can still manage.</i>

242
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:32,024
CHAE-MIN STILL HAS ENERGY

243
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:36,404
<i>This is still fine. It's okay.</i>

244
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:39,323
CAR, THE GARDEN IS SLOWLY GETTING TIRED

245
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:44,662
Nice.

246
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:49,041
Tell me anytime you want.

247
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:51,335
Or I'll say it first.

248
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,341
Does leaning for one minute
count as resting too?

249
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,509
-Okay.
-Yes.

250
00:11:58,592 --> 00:12:00,052
-That's a rest too?
-Yes.

251
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,345
Then, I want to rest.

252
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,639
NAH SAYS IT FIRST AGAIN

253
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,433
-Let's take a break.
-It's coming.

254
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:07,518
I'm starting to feel annoyed.

255
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:08,686
It's building.

256
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:12,982
My calves are starting to cramp now.

257
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:15,609
Really?

258
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:20,156
We took a lot of breaks
thanks to Producer Nah.

259
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,616
When we started to feel like this,
we took a break.

260
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:27,121
So whenever I was the only one
groaning and pausing,

261
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:28,706
you could see that I stopped.

262
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:32,626
But whenever I'd get to that point,
he'd go, "I want to rest."

263
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:37,715
So it looked like I had no choice
but to rest because of Producer Nah,

264
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:38,883
and I got to rest.

265
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:40,759
-Let's go.
-Shall we?

266
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:42,219
Yeah.

267
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:45,264
I can freely ask for these short breaks
without worrying, right?

268
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:46,682
Of course.

269
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:47,933
You can ask every minute too.

270
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,435
CONSIDERATE OF OLD NAH AND WEAK CAR

271
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:50,686
These breaks are perfect.

272
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:53,272
Just a moment to let the blood circulate.

273
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,608
Yes. Just stopping for a bit helps.

274
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,693
FIVE MINUTES LATER

275
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,987
Let me take a moment here

276
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:02,239
-to tie my shoelaces really quick.
-Sure.

277
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:04,074
I'll just tie my shoelaces.

278
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:04,992
Okay.

279
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:05,910
A DEEP EXHALE

280
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:08,329
-Did they come undone?
-Yes.

281
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,413
You don't need to know.

282
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:11,790
You only need to know
if I need to tie them.

283
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:23,928
<i>Producer Nah and Car, the garden</i>

284
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:26,096
were less exhausted than usual,

285
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,390
but they still felt tired,
so we took frequent breaks.

286
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:31,018
Car, the garden
was especially passionate this time.

287
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:32,770
He could've rested longer,

288
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:35,731
but most times he said, "Let's go now."

289
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:38,859
10:11 A.M.
700 M LEFT UNTIL JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

290
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:40,861
<i>We actually can get there soon if we push.</i>

291
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,532
Gosh, this might be the steepest hill.

292
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:49,662
Let's be honest and speak up
if you want to rest.

293
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:51,622
ENTERING AREA WITH STEEP STAIRS

294
00:13:57,294 --> 00:13:59,088
-It's here.
-Yeah.

295
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:00,005
EVEN STEEPER

296
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,507
-It's here.
-Should we rest?

297
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:02,841
Shall we take a break here?

298
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:04,635
Yes. Gosh.

299
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,096
Chae-min, you must be tired.

300
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:08,264
No, that's not it.

301
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,015
-But for one last time--
-I won this time.

302
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,100
Yes, you won.

303
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,601
You lost to Producer Nah?

304
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:13,936
FIGHTING AND WINNING BY HIMSELF

305
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:15,145
You lost in the end.

306
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,856
Before we got to the hard section,

307
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:21,819
I thought, "Let's recuperate for a bit
and set off again."

308
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:23,696
If we just climb this part, is it over?

309
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:25,573
-Pretty much.
-We're almost there.

310
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:27,366
This may be today's most grueling part.

311
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:30,661
But Chae-min, how long do we have to
keep resting for you?

312
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:31,579
AT A LOSS FOR WORDS

313
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:32,746
My sweat's already cooling.

314
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:33,914
Shall we go up?

315
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:36,041
-You…
-Okay, let's start climbing.

316
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,710
It's hard to hike with a kid.

317
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,837
I'm sorry.

318
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:42,798
I've cooled down because of you.

319
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:43,966
Should we pick up the pace?

320
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:46,760
We have our own pace too, Chae-min.

321
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,095
UNGRATEFUL OLD NAH AND WEAK CAR

322
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:50,764
Athletic people like us…

323
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:51,682
SNORTING

324
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,183
…have our own rhythm.

325
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,060
Is that so?

326
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:56,937
THE FINAL INCLINE

327
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,063
Are these actually stairs?

328
00:14:58,147 --> 00:14:59,940
-I think so.
-But they're buried under snow?

329
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:00,941
That's right.

330
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,484
SHOCKED

331
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:03,694
Gosh!

332
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:05,362
Is this a StairMaster?

333
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:06,864
ATHLETIC MAN 1 BREATHES HEAVILY

334
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,658
ATHLETIC MAN 2 BREATHES HEAVILY

335
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:13,787
CHAE-MIN IS HUMMING TO HIMSELF

336
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:15,998
This might be the end
of the steepest hill.

337
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,125
I think this is the end.

338
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,420
It feels flat now.

339
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,549
If only Chae-min didn't ask
for a break earlier…

340
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,967
Did I mess with your pace?

341
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,552
You messed up the tempo a bit.

342
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:29,637
I guess I killed it.

343
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,013
I wasn't going to mention it.

344
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:31,931
Thank you.

345
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:34,433
But please remember that
we're all athletic guys.

346
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:35,601
You win.

347
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,895
Remember that we're strong, muscular men.

348
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:39,271
Got it.

349
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:42,024
If you make sportscars go slow,

350
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,067
imagine how hard…

351
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,653
Our bodies can't cope with that.

352
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:48,197
I'm sorry. I didn't know.
I should've read the room better.

353
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,366
It's okay because you're nice.

354
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,408
That's right.

355
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:53,702
We're not scolding you or anything.

356
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:54,620
It's not a scolding.

357
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,205
<i>I used to really like him.</i>

358
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,456
<i>I really like Producer Nah.</i>

359
00:15:57,539 --> 00:16:01,126
But yesterday, he said stuff like,
"Chae-min wanted to rest.

360
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,586
We'll go easy on you.

361
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,921
We'll match your pace."

362
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:04,922
He kept saying that.

363
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:07,257
But he was the biggest problem.

364
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,511
It's hard to match their pace.

365
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:17,393
MEANWHILE, GWANEUMSA TEAM
IS STILL WALKING OVER GAEMIDEUNG

366
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:19,311
Three hundred meters.

367
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,021
CURRENT LOCATION

368
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:24,358
300 M TO SAMGAKBONG SHELTER

369
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:25,609
Let's go, Dowoon.

370
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,027
We're so close to eating food.

371
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:28,112
Fifteen minutes?

372
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:29,947
-Fifteen minutes is…
-Should we push it?

373
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,907
Let's reduce it to ten minutes.

374
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:34,952
THE BEST MOTIVATION IS HUNGER

375
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:35,995
I'm hungry.

376
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,165
-Fifteen minutes.
-Sorry?

377
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,667
Fifteen minutes. Nice.

378
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:44,837
We're almost there.

379
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:53,262
You can do it.

380
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:56,974
They're celebrities.

381
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:00,227
-You can do it!
-You can do it!

382
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:01,353
-Let's go!
-Tarzzan!

383
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:02,271
-Tarzzan!
-Let's go!

384
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,355
You're so handsome!

385
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:07,651
So this is how you get closer
through hiking.

386
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,528
I'm feeling energized.

387
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,490
Those soldiers are amazing.

388
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:16,452
I know, right? They don't even have poles.

389
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:19,038
All I remember
are the Special Forces soldiers.

390
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,373
They were so cool.

391
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:24,626
THE ENERGY THEY GOT FROM THE SOLDIERS

392
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:27,212
BOWING

393
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:33,093
SHARING THE ENERGY WITH OTHER HIKERS

394
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:34,887
This is nice.

395
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,765
I see something.

396
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:39,558
-I think we're here.
-Right.

397
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,727
We're here.

398
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:46,315
AT THE END OF THE BRUTAL ASCENT

399
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:49,693
IT FEELS LIKE A GIFT

400
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:52,946
GWANEUMSA TRAIL'S ONLY SHELTER

401
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:56,408
SAMGAKBONG SHELTER

402
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:59,620
A RESTING PLACE FOR HIKERS

403
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:03,040
WHOSE GOAL IS TO REACH BAENGNOKDAM

404
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:06,335
THEY RECUPERATE
FOR THE JOURNEY THAT REMAINS

405
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,170
AND REST WITHOUT LEAVING A TRACE

406
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,588
NO LEFTOVER RAMYEON SOUP CAMPAIGN

407
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:13,008
AND THE SYMBOL OF THIS PLACE,

408
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:16,261
SAMGAKBONG

409
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:19,598
A ROCKY PEAK FORMED BY VOLCANIC ACTIVITY

410
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:22,893
AT THE END OF THE FOREST PATH

411
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:26,063
IT SIGNALS THE BEGINNING
OF THE HIGH GROUND

412
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:27,773
THE WAY TO THE TOP

413
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:29,566
THE FINAL GATEKEEPER

414
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,820
AT THE PASSAGE TO THE TOP

415
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:36,115
BELOW, THE WATERS OF JEJU
COVERED IN A SEA OF CLOUDS

416
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:41,703
THEY WILL EAT HERE AS PLANNED

417
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:45,207
10:24 A.M.
THEY ARRIVE AT SAMGAKBONG SHELTER

418
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:46,333
We made it in three hours.

419
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:49,211
30 MINUTES EARLIER THAN EXPECTED

420
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:50,838
Let's eat quickly.

421
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:51,755
Quickly?

422
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,132
I mean, let's eat slowly.

423
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,551
IT WOULD BE A SHAME TO EAT QUICKLY HERE

424
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:58,137
OUTSIDE THE SAMGAKBONG SHELTER

425
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:01,849
SAMGAKBONG IS AT THE FRONT

426
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:05,477
AT THE BACK IS THE PERFECT SPOT
FOR LOOKING AT THE SEA OF CLOUDS

427
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:08,564
THEY PREPARE TO EAT RIGHT AWAY

428
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:12,067
TARZZAN HAS SOUPLESS INSTANT NOODLES

429
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:14,236
How does this work again?
I've done this before.

430
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:15,487
DOWOON HAS A SEAWEED SOUP MRE

431
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:16,989
-"Heater package."
-Open this first.

432
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,073
Right.

433
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:21,076
THEY QUICKLY PREPARE THE FOOD

434
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:26,915
TARZZAN'S JJAJANG RAMYEON IS READY

435
00:19:27,499 --> 00:19:28,834
Dowoon, have a bite first.

436
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:30,043
You go ahead.

437
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:31,587
STILL MAKING THE MEAL

438
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:33,881
HIS FIRST PROPER MEAL OF THE DAY

439
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,683
YUM

440
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:48,187
FOOD FROM FLAT GROUND TASTES SWEET
ON THE MOUNTAINSIDE

441
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,771
I feel much better now.

442
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,649
I was so hungry.

443
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,069
DOWOON TAKES A BITE TOO

444
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,532
YUM

445
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:02,284
-It's good.
-Yes, it's good.

446
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:05,621
It looks delicious.

447
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:06,872
This is amazing.

448
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:08,332
HOT AND STEAMING SEAWEED SOUP

449
00:20:12,502 --> 00:20:13,921
YUM

450
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,841
ANOTHER BITE

451
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:19,927
-Is it good?
-Yeah.

452
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,345
Is the seaweed soup amazing?

453
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:22,387
Try some.

454
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:23,430
It's hot.

455
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,059
EXCLAIMS

456
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,477
It's delicious, Dowoon.

457
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:33,732
Take a look at the view behind you.

458
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:37,277
Can't you see the sea of clouds?

459
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:38,320
The clouds in the sky?

460
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:39,655
THE CLOUDS ON THE HORIZON

461
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:41,114
It looks like we're on a plane.

462
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:43,951
WHO CARES ABOUT THE SEA OF CLOUDS?

463
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:47,788
TARZZAN WAS VERY HUNGRY

464
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:51,124
FINISHES EVERY LAST DROP OF THE SOUP

465
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,542
We're all done eating.

466
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:57,756
HE FINISHES HIS MEAL
BY EATING ALL OF HIS RAMYEON

467
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:04,471
MEANWHILE, SEONGPANAK TEAM
ARRIVES AT JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

468
00:21:04,554 --> 00:21:07,391
JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

469
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:08,934
Do you want to eat a gimbap roll?

470
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,894
Would you like some gimbap?

471
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,187
-Sounds good.
-Okay.

472
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,272
Thank you.

473
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:15,232
-Let's share it.
-Yes, let's share.

474
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:16,400
GIMBAP ACQUIRED

475
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,529
A BITE OF GIMBAP WHILE THE RAMYEON COOKS

476
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,119
Gimbap is the best.

477
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:29,621
Cold gimbap tastes so good.

478
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:34,876
EVEN COLD GIMBAP TASTES DELICIOUS
ON HALLASAN

479
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,503
Let me try the beef bone soup ramyeon.

480
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,965
CAR, THE GARDEN
PICKED BEEF BONE SOUP RAMYEON

481
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:42,926
It's hot.

482
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,720
Yours is really hot.

483
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:46,722
This looks impressive.

484
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:50,100
CHAE-MIN PICKED
IMPRESSIVE-LOOKING JJAJANG RAMYEON

485
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:09,703
HE FINISHES ALL OF THE SOUP

486
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:12,706
AND A BITE OF GIMBAP

487
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:14,291
I'll give this a try.

488
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:18,420
You're eating this
on top of the gimbap and ramyeon?

489
00:22:18,503 --> 00:22:20,213
-Yeah.
-Seriously…

490
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,382
Is it okay to eat this much?

491
00:22:24,217 --> 00:22:27,471
EATING A LOT DESPITE THE QUESTION

492
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:29,723
You know, he really eats a lot.

493
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:31,516
At that shelter…

494
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:35,228
he ate the seaweed soup,
the beef bone soup ramyeon,

495
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:37,064
and a roll of gimbap.

496
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:41,026
He's someone who'd never leave
any leftover ramyeon soup.

497
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:43,695
He's the epitome of that campaign.

498
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:46,239
NO LEFTOVER RAMYEON SOUP CAMPAIGN

499
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:48,658
If you want ramyeon with soup, bottoms up.

500
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,368
YOU EAT ALL OF THE RAMYEON ON HALLASAN

501
00:22:50,452 --> 00:22:51,828
I finished the soup.

502
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:56,583
CLEANING UP AFTER THEMSELVES NEATLY TOO

503
00:22:56,666 --> 00:23:00,212
Honestly, I think we can have some fun
before going to sleep tonight.

504
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:03,548
SEONGPANAK TEAM FEELS RELAXED

505
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:04,966
Let's go.

506
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:08,512
11 A.M.
THEY LEAVE JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

507
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:10,430
Nice, this is the way to the summit.

508
00:23:11,389 --> 00:23:13,850
1 HOUR AND 30 MINUTES TO BAENGNOKDAM

509
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:17,938
ESTIMATED ARRIVAL TIME
12:30 P.M.

510
00:23:18,021 --> 00:23:20,315
I think this is the perfect time to go.

511
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:22,692
There aren't many people
going up right now.

512
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:26,363
NOT MANY PEOPLE AROUND

513
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:29,116
NICE WEATHER

514
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,452
AND A SMOOTH PATH

515
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:36,832
It's fine this time.

516
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:38,208
-Right?
-Yeah.

517
00:23:38,291 --> 00:23:39,918
Isn't it like how people say

518
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:43,505
you shouldn't push yourself
when running, Producer Nah?

519
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:44,422
Right?

520
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:46,341
If you do,
you won't go running the next day.

521
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:50,762
So, this is just the right pace for us.

522
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:51,847
Right.

523
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,974
We shouldn't overdo it.

524
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:56,935
SEONGPANAK TEAM IS HIKING
WITHOUT OVERDOING IT

525
00:23:57,686 --> 00:24:00,272
Also, you're helping the other hikers.

526
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:01,398
-Do you know why?
-Why?

527
00:24:01,481 --> 00:24:04,276
Female hikers smile when they see you.

528
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:07,988
It isn't easy to make people smile
when they're hiking.

529
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:10,115
No, it's the beautiful view around us.

530
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,493
<i>You're doing something amazing.</i>

531
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:16,454
DOING SOMETHING GREAT ON HALLASAN

532
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:19,749
I think all the guys are getting
their dopamine from seeing you.

533
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,459
I'll be in charge of the men.

534
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,421
But if you're a man
who's popular with men…

535
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,131
It's the most useless thing.

536
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:31,511
We passed the 1,600 m mark.

537
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:32,554
SEONGPANAK TEAM REACHES

538
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:33,722
1,600 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

539
00:24:33,805 --> 00:24:35,015
Let's take a short rest.

540
00:24:35,098 --> 00:24:36,850
GWANEUMSA TEAM LEAVES FOR BAENGNOKDAM

541
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:38,226
Thank you.

542
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:40,478
ALREADY LOOKING EXHAUSTED

543
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:41,438
Oh, dear.

544
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:43,398
HE SPOTS SOMETHING

545
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:44,316
Oh, dear.

546
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:48,820
It's narrow here.

547
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:51,323
ENOUGH FOR ONLY ONE PERSON TO WALK THROUGH

548
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:53,617
SLIPS

549
00:24:54,784 --> 00:24:56,661
SLIPPERY DUE TO SNOW PILED UP TO THE POSTS

550
00:24:57,537 --> 00:25:00,999
TRAFFIC CAUSED BY MOVING IN SINGLE FILE

551
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:03,293
Be careful. It's slippery.

552
00:25:04,711 --> 00:25:08,715
NOT STAYING ALERT
EVEN FOR A MOMENT IS DANGEROUS

553
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:10,884
Stay to the right as much as you can.

554
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:13,428
PAST THE TRICKY, NARROW DOWNHILL PATH

555
00:25:14,137 --> 00:25:16,806
THEY ENTER A FLAT AREA AGAIN

556
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,726
We came all the way up.

557
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:20,644
Exactly.

558
00:25:20,727 --> 00:25:21,853
But we're going down again.

559
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:25,565
DOWNHILL AGAIN

560
00:25:28,068 --> 00:25:29,945
THE DOWNHILL WALK ENDS

561
00:25:30,028 --> 00:25:30,862
This is nice.

562
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:35,283
AND WHAT'S WAITING FOR THEM IS

563
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:42,540
YONGJINGAK SUSPENSION BRIDGE

564
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:47,212
CROSSING THE DEEP VALLEY
OF YONGJINGAKGYEGOK VALLEY

565
00:25:47,295 --> 00:25:49,547
IS A BRIDGE 50M LONG
AND 1,560M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

566
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,883
THE VIEW OF THE RIDGE
THAT STRETCHES TO BAENGNOKDAM

567
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:54,928
BUT IT SWAYS, SO BE CAREFUL

568
00:25:57,138 --> 00:25:59,391
APPROACHING YONGJINGAK SUSPENSION BRIDGE

569
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:02,978
LAUGHING

570
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:05,397
They're giving us a thumbs up.

571
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:10,026
WHILE PASSING THE FRIENDLY HIKERS

572
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,823
THE BRIDGE SUDDENLY STARTS SWAYING

573
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,866
-Wait, Dowoon.
-What?

574
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:18,868
The bridge is shaking.

575
00:26:18,952 --> 00:26:20,662
I have a fear of heights.

576
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:22,372
THIS BRIDGE

577
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:24,708
IS HANGING HIGH ABOVE THE VALLEY

578
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:27,210
IT ALSO SHAKES
AND MAY TRIGGER A FEAR OF HEIGHTS

579
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,587
Slow down.

580
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:30,922
Don't look down.

581
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:32,215
Look up.

582
00:26:33,049 --> 00:26:34,092
SCARED

583
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:36,052
SLOWLY

584
00:26:36,136 --> 00:26:39,055
SUDDEN DECREASE IN SPEED

585
00:26:39,139 --> 00:26:40,473
Want to hold onto the railing?

586
00:26:41,599 --> 00:26:42,642
Take your time.

587
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:45,645
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

588
00:26:45,729 --> 00:26:46,688
SPOOKED

589
00:26:47,731 --> 00:26:50,608
DIFFICULTY FOR MOST: EASY
DIFFICULTY FOR TARZZAN: HARD

590
00:26:50,692 --> 00:26:53,194
CAN'T TAKE HIS EYES OFF OF HIM

591
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:54,863
<i>You crossed the shaky bridge.</i>

592
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:56,990
<i>Do you remember the view from there?</i>

593
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:58,992
The view? No, I don't remember.

594
00:26:59,075 --> 00:27:00,535
ALL HE SAW WAS A SCARED TARZZAN

595
00:27:00,618 --> 00:27:02,579
Chae-won was a bit scared.

596
00:27:02,662 --> 00:27:04,164
He has a fear of heights.

597
00:27:04,247 --> 00:27:06,291
But if that's the case,
Chae-won is amazing.

598
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:08,293
Hallasan is really high.

599
00:27:08,376 --> 00:27:10,211
He must've been scared,
but he overcame it.

600
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:12,172
QUICKLY CHANGING IT TO A COMPLIMENT

601
00:27:12,255 --> 00:27:14,841
I didn't know
the bridge would shake so much.

602
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:16,468
I survived.

603
00:27:17,177 --> 00:27:18,428
He's so cute.

604
00:27:18,511 --> 00:27:21,348
THEY ARRIVE SAFELY

605
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:25,310
I'm most scared of those kinds of bridges
and transparent elevators.

606
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:28,772
AS SOON AS THEY CROSS THE BRIDGE,
IT'S AN UPHILL WALK AGAIN

607
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:30,732
That's Baengnokdam over there.

608
00:27:30,815 --> 00:27:32,609
-Where?
-It's in front of you.

609
00:27:35,653 --> 00:27:37,155
FACING A NOW NEARBY BAENGNOKDAM

610
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:39,783
THE REAL CHALLENGE STARTS NOW

611
00:27:39,866 --> 00:27:42,118
CURRENT LOCATION

612
00:27:42,702 --> 00:27:46,581
NOT THE BEST PLACE
TO CATCH THEIR BREATHS

613
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,752
AN ENDLESS STRETCH
OF STEEP STAIRS FOR AN HOUR

614
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:53,421
NOTORIOUS FOR MAKING HIKERS BREATHLESS

615
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:55,423
WANGGWANREUNG

616
00:27:56,007 --> 00:27:59,636
THE FINAL STRETCH OF HELLISH STAIRS
TO BAENGNOKDAM

617
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:04,140
ENTERING THE GATES OF HELL

618
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:11,398
RECHARGING HIMSELF WITH GUMMIES
FROM THE START

619
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:13,233
<i>You ate them as you walked.</i>

620
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:16,361
Yes, it's like when you drive
for five hours or so.

621
00:28:16,444 --> 00:28:18,571
You keep eating snacks without thinking.

622
00:28:18,655 --> 00:28:19,948
It's something like that.

623
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:22,659
ON THE STEEP PATH

624
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:25,161
HE FUELS HIMSELF WITH GUMMIES

625
00:28:25,245 --> 00:28:27,080
STARTING HIS ENGINE

626
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:31,501
ACCELERATES

627
00:28:31,584 --> 00:28:32,544
PANTING

628
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:35,130
SLOWS DOWN

629
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:39,217
ACCELERATES AGAIN

630
00:28:40,427 --> 00:28:43,805
ALTERNATING BETWEEN ACCELERATING
AND SLOWING DOWN

631
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:45,849
It's 5-28.

632
00:28:45,932 --> 00:28:46,808
Damn it.

633
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,352
SIX SECTIONS LEFT
UNTIL BAENGNOKDAM AT 5-34

634
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:52,021
1.5 KM LEFT

635
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:54,232
GRUNTING

636
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:55,650
DEEP EXHALE

637
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:56,818
TRUDGING

638
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,903
Stairs like these…

639
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:01,364
We're going to cross
an endless stretch of stairs now.

640
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:03,783
If you get tired halfway, you can rest.
Let us know.

641
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:04,701
Okay.

642
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:05,785
-Tell us.
-Okay.

643
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:07,078
It's a very steep hill here.

644
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,621
The hardest part will appear soon.

645
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,165
THIS IS JUST THE ENTRANCE

646
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:14,169
MEANWHILE, TARZZAN IS HAVING
AN ESPECIALLY HARD TIME

647
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:19,883
HE TAKES OUT THE GUMMIES AGAIN

648
00:29:23,845 --> 00:29:26,306
THEY SHARE THE GUMMIES

649
00:29:26,389 --> 00:29:29,601
SETTING OFF AGAIN

650
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:31,352
YUM

651
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:32,729
<i>The gummies helped a lot.</i>

652
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:34,147
<i>The ones Dowoon gave me.</i>

653
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:38,193
You know, when I ate one
just as I wanted to take a break…

654
00:29:39,235 --> 00:29:40,862
<i>I could see clearly again.</i>

655
00:29:41,529 --> 00:29:42,614
YUM

656
00:29:42,697 --> 00:29:47,494
BOOST FROM GUMMIES ACTIVATE

657
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:50,121
THEY KEEP WALKING

658
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:53,208
INCLINE SO STEEP
ONLY TOPS OF HEADS ARE SEEN BEHIND YOU

659
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:56,753
CLIMBING ALMOST VERTICALLY

660
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:05,678
THE HIKERS IN FRONT OF THEM
ARE TAKING A SHORT BREAK

661
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:11,434
PANTING AND WALKING PAST THEM

662
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:14,854
Damn.

663
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:16,981
This is no joke.

664
00:30:18,608 --> 00:30:19,526
Gosh.

665
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:29,661
EVEN THOUGH THEY'RE TIRED,
THEY CONTINUE HIKING

666
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:30,912
EXHALING

667
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:34,582
THEY KEEP WALKING
WITHOUT ASKING FOR A BREAK

668
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:37,544
11:38 A.M.
THEY REACH 1,600M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

669
00:30:37,627 --> 00:30:41,339
THE INCLINE GETS STEEPER WITH ALTITUDE

670
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:46,469
THOSE GOING DOWN ARE STRUGGLING TOO

671
00:30:48,847 --> 00:30:50,473
<i>There were too many uphill sections.</i>

672
00:30:50,557 --> 00:30:52,350
<i>It was an uphill climb all the way.</i>

673
00:30:52,433 --> 00:30:55,019
I think everything after the shelter
was hard.

674
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:55,937
Yes.

675
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,105
It was all hard for me.

676
00:30:57,188 --> 00:31:00,567
But we actually passed
a lot of hikers on the way.

677
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:01,651
Right.

678
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:06,155
THEY HIKED WITHOUT RESTING

679
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:08,658
BETWEEN RESTING HIKERS

680
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:12,996
PASSING BY

681
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:17,333
PASSING BY AGAIN

682
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:20,044
EVEN AFTER THAT…

683
00:31:27,969 --> 00:31:29,929
THEY KEPT WALKING WITHOUT RESTING

684
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:36,311
NO STRENGTH TO EVEN LIFT HIS HEAD

685
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:41,107
MESSY HAIR

686
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:44,777
THE PRODUCTION CREW DIDN'T REST EITHER

687
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:45,987
Let's rest for 30 seconds.

688
00:31:46,070 --> 00:31:47,530
The camera operators need to rest.

689
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:48,948
Okay.

690
00:31:49,657 --> 00:31:52,660
THE PRODUCTION CREW HASN'T RESTED YET
AND WILL REGROUP FOR A BIT

691
00:31:53,453 --> 00:31:54,412
This is no joke.

692
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:55,872
CAN PAUSE THANKS TO THEM

693
00:31:55,955 --> 00:31:57,165
Gosh.

694
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,000
There's no end to them.

695
00:31:59,083 --> 00:32:01,628
<i>You rested a few times because I asked to,</i>

696
00:32:01,711 --> 00:32:02,962
<i>but otherwise, you kept going.</i>

697
00:32:03,046 --> 00:32:04,589
Whenever I climb up, I think,

698
00:32:04,672 --> 00:32:08,384
"Once I stop,
I won't be able to move again."

699
00:32:08,468 --> 00:32:09,719
I want to keep resting.

700
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:11,763
And everyone hikes so well

701
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:13,473
that I feel bad asking to stop.

702
00:32:13,556 --> 00:32:15,516
Everyone walks so fast in front of me.

703
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:16,935
So that's what it was.

704
00:32:17,018 --> 00:32:19,187
You kept going without resting,

705
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:20,897
so I thought, "He's so fit."

706
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:22,231
Honestly, we were dying too.

707
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:24,400
But nobody showed it.

708
00:32:24,484 --> 00:32:25,318
-Really?
-Yes.

709
00:32:25,401 --> 00:32:26,903
It must've been tough.

710
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:30,073
Honestly, we just need to
carry our own stuff.

711
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:32,951
But everyone else, like our sound mixer…

712
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:34,953
How heavy was it again?

713
00:32:35,036 --> 00:32:36,454
-Was it 25 kg?
-That's right.

714
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:38,206
Our camera operator in front of me…

715
00:32:38,289 --> 00:32:39,123
Deok-hwan.

716
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:41,376
A former Special Forces soldier?

717
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:42,627
He was impressive too.

718
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:45,171
I realized I really shouldn't complain.

719
00:32:45,254 --> 00:32:47,256
THEY DIDN'T STOP
SO THE CREW DOESN'T SUFFER

720
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:57,433
Are you done? Give it to me.

721
00:32:58,101 --> 00:32:59,394
Here. Drink this.

722
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:00,728
-Thank you.
-No worries.

723
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:02,563
CATCHING THEIR BREATHS WITH A SIP OF WATER

724
00:33:02,647 --> 00:33:04,232
I miss Car, the garden.

725
00:33:04,315 --> 00:33:05,733
Me too. He would've collapsed here.

726
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:08,027
THE TOUGH TRAIL
REMINDS THEM OF THEIR WEAKEST FRIEND

727
00:33:09,612 --> 00:33:13,074
CAR, THE GARDEN IS GOING STRONG

728
00:33:14,617 --> 00:33:16,327
The snow is melting here.

729
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:21,708
Look to your left.

730
00:33:24,168 --> 00:33:26,129
Look to your left.

731
00:33:27,296 --> 00:33:28,423
What's that?

732
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:31,926
It's so beautiful.

733
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:33,344
That's incredible.

734
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:36,222
THE SEA OF CLOUDS IN FRONT OF THEM

735
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:38,474
Just a moment. I'd like to take a picture.

736
00:33:43,563 --> 00:33:44,689
Good luck.

737
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:47,984
It's so beautiful.

738
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:51,696
Jung-won, let me take your photo.

739
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:52,989
Okay.

740
00:33:58,161 --> 00:33:59,162
It's really beautiful.

741
00:33:59,746 --> 00:34:01,914
It feels like I'm above the clouds.

742
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:09,047
This is amazing.

743
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:10,548
THEY GET THE BEST VIEW
OF THE CLOUDS

744
00:34:10,631 --> 00:34:11,758
<i>It was like a painting.</i>

745
00:34:11,841 --> 00:34:16,387
You got the view
of Jeju Island next to the sea,

746
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:18,514
and there was a bunch
of clouds above that.

747
00:34:18,598 --> 00:34:22,268
It felt like Hallasan was welcoming us.

748
00:34:23,936 --> 00:34:27,023
THE VIEW THAT HALLASAN WELCOMES YOU WITH

749
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,693
This is unbelievable.

750
00:34:31,527 --> 00:34:32,612
No way.

751
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:41,245
I get to see this view
thanks to this show.

752
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:43,247
Good job, Chae-min.

753
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:46,626
Are you feeling good this time?

754
00:34:46,709 --> 00:34:47,543
No.

755
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:49,003
NEGATIVE GARDEN SHOWS UP INSTANTLY

756
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,838
Jung-won, you're slowly becoming negative.

757
00:34:50,922 --> 00:34:52,340
No, it's because I'm so happy.

758
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:54,342
I can't even talk.

759
00:34:56,886 --> 00:34:58,888
MEANWHILE, GWANEUMSA TEAM
REALLY CAN'T TALK

760
00:34:58,971 --> 00:35:00,431
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

761
00:35:01,682 --> 00:35:03,810
Deok-hwan must be dying.

762
00:35:03,893 --> 00:35:06,646
This is pretty much like
military training.

763
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:10,566
Just now,

764
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:11,901
a hiker was behind me.

765
00:35:11,984 --> 00:35:13,986
I said, "We're filming,
so you can go first."

766
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:16,447
And they said, "No, I want to rest too."

767
00:35:16,531 --> 00:35:17,532
It was a total stranger.

768
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:20,409
That's so cute.

769
00:35:20,493 --> 00:35:21,786
"No!"

770
00:35:21,869 --> 00:35:22,870
A DESPERATE REQUEST

771
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:27,542
That means it's not just us.
Everyone else…

772
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:28,584
Everyone is…

773
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:30,211
THOSE AT THE BACK PAUSE TOO

774
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:31,796
Everyone is passing out.

775
00:35:31,879 --> 00:35:35,716
THOSE IN FRONT
STRUGGLE TO MOVE FORWARD AS WELL

776
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:37,218
Let's go.

777
00:35:37,301 --> 00:35:39,846
THEY KEEP CLIMBING

778
00:35:41,097 --> 00:35:43,850
11:45 A.M.
THEY PASS 5-29

779
00:35:43,933 --> 00:35:47,603
FIVE LEFT UNTIL 5-34 AND BAENGNOKDAM

780
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:50,815
THEY'RE AT EYE LEVEL WITH BAENGNOKDAM NOW

781
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,693
-We're almost there.
-Wait, are we really here?

782
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:56,279
-You are.
-Thank you.

783
00:35:57,738 --> 00:36:00,449
THEY JUST NEED TO CLIMB UP
THE REMAINING STAIRS

784
00:36:01,367 --> 00:36:04,453
TO ARRIVE AT AN OPEN CLEARING

785
00:36:04,537 --> 00:36:08,624
CURRENT LOCATION
WANGGWANREUNG HELIPORT

786
00:36:08,708 --> 00:36:11,711
LOCATED ON THE RIDGE
RIGHT NEXT TO WANGGWANREUNG

787
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:14,839
A HELIPORT
FOR EMERGENCY TRANSPORT AND SEARCH

788
00:36:16,507 --> 00:36:19,385
GWANEUMSA TRAIL'S FINAL REST AREA
BEFORE BAENGNOKDAM

789
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:20,803
Tarzzan.

790
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:22,388
Good luck. You can do it.

791
00:36:22,471 --> 00:36:24,056
-Thank you.
-You can do it.

792
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:25,516
Thank you.

793
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:28,102
HE ARRIVES AT THE HELIPORT
WHILE BEING CHEERED

794
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:30,146
-Dowoon.
-This is crazy.

795
00:36:31,439 --> 00:36:33,274
A BIT EARLY BUT A HIGH-FIVE TO CELEBRATE

796
00:36:33,357 --> 00:36:35,026
I'm so exhausted.

797
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,612
Where is Baengnokdam?

798
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:39,697
Over there.

799
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:40,907
We need to go there.

800
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:41,949
That is Baengnokdam.

801
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,159
BAENGNOKDAM

802
00:36:44,243 --> 00:36:45,369
There's a lot left to go.

803
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:47,538
SIGHS

804
00:36:47,622 --> 00:36:50,666
I'm really running out of stamina now.

805
00:36:51,667 --> 00:36:52,919
What's "seminar"?

806
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:54,086
I said, "stamina."

807
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:55,254
Oh, stamina.

808
00:36:55,338 --> 00:36:57,215
HE NEVER CHANGES

809
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:59,008
My stamina is just…

810
00:36:59,091 --> 00:37:02,053
AND ANOTHER PERSON
WHO'S RUNNING OUT OF STAMINA HERE

811
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:03,387
Look at Seon-u.

812
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:05,223
It's summertime for him.

813
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,100
THE MAN WITH THE 25 KG BAG

814
00:37:08,684 --> 00:37:10,394
LAUGHING

815
00:37:10,478 --> 00:37:12,772
Seriously though,
you'll succeed in everything you do.

816
00:37:13,356 --> 00:37:16,067
You're so mentally strong.

817
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:19,779
Seriously, he'll succeed
in anything he tries.

818
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:23,783
This show pushes the production crew
to their limits.

819
00:37:24,325 --> 00:37:26,285
They have my full respect.

820
00:37:28,829 --> 00:37:29,747
The last bit.

821
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:31,540
It'll take about 30 to 40 minutes.

822
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:32,750
ABOUT 1.25 KM TO BAENGNOKDAM

823
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:37,213
11:51 A.M.
THEY DEPART WANGGWANREUNG HELIPORT

824
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:39,215
Look at the clouds.

825
00:37:39,298 --> 00:37:40,174
Gosh.

826
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:42,551
Gosh, the clouds. Over there.

827
00:37:42,635 --> 00:37:44,053
They're below us. Look back there.

828
00:37:44,136 --> 00:37:46,264
THEY GET A SENSE OF THE ELEVATION
FROM THE VIEW

829
00:37:46,347 --> 00:37:48,849
Aside from planes,
I haven't been anywhere this high before.

830
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:50,935
BUT IT'S TOO SOON TO BE SURPRISED

831
00:37:51,018 --> 00:37:53,229
THEIR DESTINATION, BAENGNOKDAM,

832
00:37:53,312 --> 00:37:56,023
IS THE HIGHEST PLACE YOU CAN SET FOOT ON

833
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:59,360
SINCE IT'S RIGHT IN FRONT OF THEM,
THERE'S NOT MUCH DISTANCE LEFT

834
00:37:59,443 --> 00:38:01,028
GROANING

835
00:38:01,112 --> 00:38:02,363
Damn it.

836
00:38:02,446 --> 00:38:05,241
THE PROBLEM IS
THEY DON'T HAVE MUCH STAMINA LEFT EITHER

837
00:38:08,369 --> 00:38:09,620
It's 5-30.

838
00:38:11,163 --> 00:38:14,250
11:56 A.M.
THEY PASS 5-30

839
00:38:14,333 --> 00:38:17,920
REMAINING DISTANCE IS 1 KM

840
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:22,800
Damn it.

841
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:24,343
GROANS

842
00:38:25,052 --> 00:38:26,137
EXHALING

843
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:27,305
DEEP BREATH

844
00:38:27,388 --> 00:38:31,309
A DUET OF GROANING CONTINUES

845
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:34,979
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM
DOESN'T EVEN HAVE TIME TO LOOK BACK

846
00:38:35,062 --> 00:38:35,896
It's so beautiful.

847
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,732
SEONGPANAK TEAM ENJOYS
THE VIEW BEHIND THEM

848
00:38:37,815 --> 00:38:39,567
I bet it'll look beautiful on Baengnokdam.

849
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:41,277
Is that Baengnokdam?

850
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:42,778
Yes, it's up there.

851
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:44,822
We came up really high.

852
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:46,824
BAENGNOKDAM

853
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:48,492
We're almost there, but it looks high.

854
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:50,494
This is so beautiful.

855
00:38:52,288 --> 00:38:54,040
It's so nice
that I don't regret coming up.

856
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,541
BAENGNOKDAM IS RIGHT AHEAD

857
00:38:57,501 --> 00:38:58,502
<i>What a nice view.</i>

858
00:38:58,586 --> 00:39:02,965
THEY HIKE WITH THE SEA OF CLOUDS
BEHIND THEM

859
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:04,759
This is incredible. It feels like the US.

860
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:06,177
THE VIEW IS INCREDIBLY STUNNING

861
00:39:06,260 --> 00:39:08,387
REACHING FOR HIS POCKETS

862
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:16,937
UNBELIEVABLY, CAR, THE GARDEN
TAKES A PICTURE

863
00:39:17,021 --> 00:39:18,147
This looks pretty nice.

864
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:21,442
You don't get many chances like this.

865
00:39:21,525 --> 00:39:22,818
HALLASAN MAKES CAR TAKE PICTURES

866
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:26,947
Usually, all you can see is the trail.

867
00:39:27,031 --> 00:39:28,115
The rest is covered in fog.

868
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,283
-Really?
-Usually.

869
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:30,993
If that was the case today,

870
00:39:31,077 --> 00:39:33,162
I would've felt so annoyed.

871
00:39:33,245 --> 00:39:34,080
Right.

872
00:39:34,163 --> 00:39:35,623
-Seriously.
-Yeah, after all that.

873
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:37,041
A FOGGY HALLASAN SOUNDS TERRIBLE

874
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:38,667
Actually, I don't feel annoyed today.

875
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:41,128
I feel good.

876
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:44,423
We have 800m to go.

877
00:39:47,551 --> 00:39:50,846
LET'S HAPPILY HIKE
THE REMAINING 800M TO THE TOP!

878
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:05,903
BOTH THE SNOWY PATH
AND WOODEN STAIRS

879
00:40:05,986 --> 00:40:07,071
I can see the end.

880
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:09,156
Hallasan.

881
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:10,574
Let's settle things today.

882
00:40:15,204 --> 00:40:17,456
It saps your energy one last time.

883
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:19,542
Gosh, this is so…

884
00:40:20,334 --> 00:40:21,919
nice.

885
00:40:22,002 --> 00:40:23,212
I'm happy.

886
00:40:24,046 --> 00:40:25,339
I'm so happy.

887
00:40:25,423 --> 00:40:26,674
HE DOESN'T MEAN IT

888
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:34,098
The path is paved really well here,
but it still feels a bit like Seoraksan.

889
00:40:34,181 --> 00:40:35,099
I agree.

890
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:38,894
It's basalt.

891
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:46,068
THE FIRST HURDLE RIGHT BEFORE THE SUMMIT
A BASALT SLOPE

892
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:50,948
AS EXPECTED OF JEJU ISLAND,
THE ROCKY PATH IS MADE OF BASALT

893
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:00,583
There are rocks at the end?

894
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:01,792
That makes me angry.

895
00:41:04,044 --> 00:41:05,880
It's so steep here.

896
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:08,674
This section is tough.

897
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:13,387
THE LONGEST AND MOST BRUTAL PATH
OF SEONGPANAK

898
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:15,639
We've walked so much
but still haven't reached.

899
00:41:16,807 --> 00:41:18,726
Just when you think it'll end, it doesn't.

900
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,394
THE STEEP PATH NEVER ENDS

901
00:41:22,229 --> 00:41:23,772
Are we here? This last part is rough.

902
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:25,774
HOLDING ONTO THE ROPE AS THEY SLOWLY CLIMB

903
00:41:26,358 --> 00:41:27,610
<i>There are a lot of people.</i>

904
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:30,279
<i>There are so many people up here.</i>

905
00:41:30,362 --> 00:41:33,240
THE SECOND HURDLE RIGHT BEFORE THE SUMMIT
ONE PATH BUT MANY PEOPLE

906
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:39,038
THE CLOSER YOU ARE TO THE SUMMIT,
THE MORE PEOPLE YOU FIND

907
00:41:39,121 --> 00:41:41,040
It's so cold.

908
00:41:41,123 --> 00:41:42,500
I need my padded jacket.

909
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:46,879
THE THIRD HURDLE
COLD WIND

910
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:49,173
It's cold now that we're up here.

911
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:53,385
AS THE HIGHEST MOUNTAIN IN KOREA,
IT GETS COLDER THE HIGHER YOU CLIMB

912
00:41:55,221 --> 00:41:56,889
Are they actually lined up?

913
00:41:56,972 --> 00:41:59,225
They're in line to take pictures
of the summit marker.

914
00:42:01,393 --> 00:42:02,811
Really? That's crazy.

915
00:42:07,233 --> 00:42:10,027
A FEW STEPS AWAY
FROM THE SUMMIT OF HALLASAN

916
00:42:11,445 --> 00:42:14,823
WILL THEY HAVE
A CLEAR VIEW OF BAENGNOKDAM?

917
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:19,161
Is this it?

918
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:21,330
Amazing.

919
00:42:39,014 --> 00:42:42,935
BAENGNOKDAM

920
00:42:49,441 --> 00:42:50,943
THEY FINALLY MEET A CLEAR BAENGNOKDAM

921
00:42:51,026 --> 00:42:52,361
This so nice.

922
00:42:54,738 --> 00:42:56,365
What is this?

923
00:42:56,448 --> 00:42:58,534
The crater of a volcano.

924
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:03,706
CRATER FORMED ABOUT 16,000 YEARS AGO

925
00:43:04,915 --> 00:43:08,043
LOCATED 1,950M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

926
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:14,216
THE CRATER LAKE AT THE SUMMIT OF HALLASAN

927
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:18,429
CONSISTS OF VARIOUS VOLCANIC ROCKS,
SUCH AS BASALT AND TRACHYTE

928
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:22,433
DESIGNATED AS SCENIC SITE NUMBER 90

929
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:35,070
THE PLACE CLOSEST TO THE SKY

930
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:44,538
<i>They say you need three generations</i>
<i>of luck to see Baengnokdam.</i>

931
00:43:46,123 --> 00:43:49,043
I guess some people
must've done a lot of good deeds.

932
00:43:49,126 --> 00:43:52,630
But I think all of this
was thanks to the production crew.

933
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:55,966
It was thanks to the unsung heroes.

934
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:59,053
Thanks to our producers, we got to see it.

935
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:05,893
It's beautiful.

936
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:07,811
It is pretty cool.

937
00:44:07,895 --> 00:44:09,730
HE TAKES A PICTURE BECAUSE IT'S COOL

938
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:14,193
<i>It was a bit of a shame</i>
<i>since the lake wasn't there,</i>

939
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:16,278
<i>but it was still beautiful.</i>

940
00:44:17,905 --> 00:44:21,659
"HEAVENLY HERMITS COME DOWN TO BAENGNOKDAM
RIDING WHITE DEER TO DRINK WATER"

941
00:44:21,742 --> 00:44:23,035
IMHAPILGI<i>,</i> 1871

942
00:44:25,913 --> 00:44:29,416
WHEN THE SNOW MELTS,
IT TURNS INTO A CLEAR LAKE

943
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:33,545
BAENGNOKDAM TAKES ON MANY FORMS

944
00:44:41,929 --> 00:44:44,390
SEONGPANAK TEAM REACHES BAENGNOKDAM
IN 4 HOURS AND 30 MINUTES

945
00:44:44,473 --> 00:44:45,974
It feels cold now.

946
00:44:46,934 --> 00:44:49,395
Are Tarzzan and the others not here yet?

947
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:50,813
Why aren't they here?

948
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:58,445
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM IS STILL ON ITS WAY

949
00:45:04,993 --> 00:45:06,829
-Damn it.
-Can we take a photo?

950
00:45:06,912 --> 00:45:07,996
Okay.

951
00:45:09,456 --> 00:45:10,499
GROANING

952
00:45:11,208 --> 00:45:12,084
GRUNTS

953
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:14,002
One, two, three.

954
00:45:14,586 --> 00:45:17,172
A PHOTO WITH THE SEA OF CLOUDS BEHIND THEM

955
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:22,386
AFTER TAKING A PHOTO,
THEY RESUME CLIMBING UP

956
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:26,348
12:12 P.M.
THEY PASS 5-32

957
00:45:26,432 --> 00:45:28,725
ONLY 500M LEFT TO BAENGNOKDAM

958
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:30,436
Damn it.

959
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:31,645
Geez.

960
00:45:32,146 --> 00:45:33,480
Damn it.

961
00:45:33,564 --> 00:45:34,898
Geez.

962
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:40,112
THE GROANING DUET STARTS AGAIN

963
00:45:40,195 --> 00:45:41,405
Damn it.

964
00:45:42,489 --> 00:45:43,532
GROANS

965
00:45:44,199 --> 00:45:46,702
THE GROANING SOLO CONTINUES AS WELL

966
00:45:46,785 --> 00:45:49,413
<i>You kept cursing, Dowoon.</i>

967
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:51,540
I didn't go that far.

968
00:45:51,623 --> 00:45:53,041
The furthest I went was "Damn it."

969
00:45:53,125 --> 00:45:54,334
I really did quit swearing.

970
00:45:54,418 --> 00:45:55,669
It's like this.

971
00:45:55,752 --> 00:45:59,715
When people work in the fields,
they say stuff like "heave-ho."

972
00:45:59,798 --> 00:46:00,924
That's what it is.

973
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:04,928
ENTERING THE LAST SET OF WOODEN STAIRS

974
00:46:05,512 --> 00:46:08,849
AS THEY SPEED UP

975
00:46:09,475 --> 00:46:11,310
The Seongpanak team has just arrived.

976
00:46:11,393 --> 00:46:12,227
What?

977
00:46:12,311 --> 00:46:14,062
We should arrive in ten minutes too.

978
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,230
They arrived already?

979
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,774
SEONGPANAK TEAM
ARRIVED EARLIER THAN EXPECTED

980
00:46:17,858 --> 00:46:20,777
Hey, that was faster than this trail.

981
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:23,071
We weren't going slow at all though.

982
00:46:23,155 --> 00:46:24,156
No, we're going fast.

983
00:46:24,239 --> 00:46:26,492
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM IS 30 MINUTES EARLY TOO

984
00:46:26,575 --> 00:46:28,243
It's 5-33.

985
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:30,913
There's only one left until 5-34.

986
00:46:30,996 --> 00:46:32,748
5 HOURS PASSED, 12:26 P.M.
THEY PASS 5-33

987
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:34,374
How many meters was it between signs?

988
00:46:34,458 --> 00:46:35,542
It's 250 meters.

989
00:46:48,972 --> 00:46:49,806
You're almost there.

990
00:46:49,890 --> 00:46:50,724
Gosh, thank you.

991
00:46:50,807 --> 00:46:52,392
That's the summit.

992
00:46:52,476 --> 00:46:54,102
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

993
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:58,649
THE LAST FLIGHT OF STAIRS

994
00:46:59,983 --> 00:47:01,109
We're here.

995
00:47:02,152 --> 00:47:03,153
Damn it.

996
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,364
Damn it.

997
00:47:14,581 --> 00:47:16,208
GWANEUMSA TEAM ARRIVES AT BAENGNOKDAM

998
00:47:19,253 --> 00:47:22,673
CURRENT TIME
12:30 P.M.

999
00:47:24,132 --> 00:47:27,636
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM
COMPLETES THEIR GOAL IN SILENCE

1000
00:47:28,220 --> 00:47:29,846
THEY HEAD STRAIGHT TO SEE BAENGNOKDAM

1001
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:31,390
There's no water.

1002
00:47:31,473 --> 00:47:32,432
The water froze.

1003
00:47:32,933 --> 00:47:34,434
-That's supposed to be water?
-Yes.

1004
00:47:36,728 --> 00:47:38,480
BAENGNOKDAM IS FROZEN WHITE IN WINTER

1005
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:39,773
I'll take a photo.

1006
00:47:39,856 --> 00:47:40,732
Sure.

1007
00:47:40,816 --> 00:47:45,654
A RARE INSTANCE
OF VOLUNTEERING TO TAKE A PHOTO

1008
00:47:45,737 --> 00:47:48,657
PICTURES OF THEMSELVES FOLLOW

1009
00:47:48,740 --> 00:47:53,245
THEY EACH HURRIEDLY TAKE A PHOTO
TO PROVE THEY WERE THERE

1010
00:47:54,162 --> 00:47:55,664
Let's go to where the others are.

1011
00:47:56,331 --> 00:47:59,126
THEY GO TO FIND THE SEONGPANAK TEAM

1012
00:48:00,419 --> 00:48:04,798
THEY QUICKLY FIND THEM

1013
00:48:05,716 --> 00:48:07,718
Gosh, I'm so angry!

1014
00:48:08,468 --> 00:48:10,429
Hey, good job.

1015
00:48:10,512 --> 00:48:12,431
WELCOME

1016
00:48:12,514 --> 00:48:14,850
-I'm so mad!
-Why?

1017
00:48:14,933 --> 00:48:17,185
I'm not lying when I say this.

1018
00:48:17,269 --> 00:48:18,854
Our trail was Seoraksan Part Two.

1019
00:48:18,937 --> 00:48:20,022
-Really?
-Yes.

1020
00:48:20,105 --> 00:48:20,939
That bad?

1021
00:48:21,023 --> 00:48:23,275
We said if you were with us,
you would've quit the show.

1022
00:48:23,358 --> 00:48:24,568
That would be true.

1023
00:48:24,651 --> 00:48:26,153
Why give us such hard trails?

1024
00:48:26,236 --> 00:48:28,905
I mean, even in running,
they say to take it easy when you start.

1025
00:48:30,657 --> 00:48:31,658
-It was intense.
-Really?

1026
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:33,368
Why do you make it so hard for us?

1027
00:48:33,452 --> 00:48:34,953
Honestly, our path wasn't that hard.

1028
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:35,912
Really?

1029
00:48:35,996 --> 00:48:36,955
It was like Taebaeksan.

1030
00:48:37,039 --> 00:48:39,333
Taebaeksan? Ours was like Seoraksan.

1031
00:48:39,416 --> 00:48:40,751
Ours was like Seoraksan.

1032
00:48:40,834 --> 00:48:42,961
-Man, at the end…
-Like Seoraksan?

1033
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:45,422
WHAT WAS IT LIKE WHEN YOU MET THEM?

1034
00:48:45,505 --> 00:48:47,215
I thought it must've been tough for them.

1035
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:48,717
Yes.

1036
00:48:49,551 --> 00:48:51,845
Jung-won definitely looked happy.

1037
00:48:51,928 --> 00:48:55,390
He seemed to be in good condition,
which was good.

1038
00:48:55,474 --> 00:49:00,103
But to be honest,
all of them were injured,

1039
00:49:00,187 --> 00:49:01,772
so I couldn't be mad at them.

1040
00:49:01,855 --> 00:49:03,023
So…

1041
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:06,193
Well, if you're still alive,
you have to carry on.

1042
00:49:08,111 --> 00:49:11,114
"It was like Seoraksan."
The moment I heard that, I could imagine.

1043
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:12,741
"I see. Okay."

1044
00:49:13,408 --> 00:49:14,993
I resented the production crew a bit.

1045
00:49:15,702 --> 00:49:18,622
Since my wrist was hurt,
I resented you.

1046
00:49:19,206 --> 00:49:20,874
But then, I became grateful.

1047
00:49:21,708 --> 00:49:24,211
Should I set the timer
for nine minutes now?

1048
00:49:24,294 --> 00:49:26,838
PROMISE ONE: DESCEND IN 9 MINUTES

1049
00:49:27,798 --> 00:49:29,800
Okay, let's take a photo.

1050
00:49:29,883 --> 00:49:31,677
The older guys
make a big heart in the back.

1051
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:33,553
The younger guys
sit and make a small one.

1052
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:35,013
Let's take it quickly.

1053
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:38,016
SUMMIT PROMISE TWO:
TAKE A GROUP PHOTO

1054
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:41,353
Look as happy as you can.
Where do we look?

1055
00:49:41,436 --> 00:49:42,604
-At me.
-Okay.

1056
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:47,484
Oh, here.

1057
00:49:48,193 --> 00:49:49,027
Two, three…

1058
00:49:54,408 --> 00:49:58,954
FEBRUARY 4, 2026
AT BAENGNOKDAM, HALLASAN

1059
00:49:59,037 --> 00:50:00,330
I achieved my goal.

1060
00:50:00,414 --> 00:50:01,832
THE ONE WHO SUGGESTED A GROUP PHOTO

1061
00:50:01,915 --> 00:50:07,170
A warm and happy photo of us
that's nice enough to put up on my fridge.

1062
00:50:07,254 --> 00:50:10,507
It's like how you take
four-cut photos with your friends.

1063
00:50:10,590 --> 00:50:12,592
I wanted to do something like that.

1064
00:50:12,676 --> 00:50:16,513
I've already become attached
to the others.

1065
00:50:17,264 --> 00:50:18,849
We've gone through hardships together.

1066
00:50:19,433 --> 00:50:20,767
I was happy with it.

1067
00:50:22,728 --> 00:50:24,104
Okay, let's go.

1068
00:50:24,187 --> 00:50:26,356
-Let's go.
-But Baengnokdam isn't in the photo.

1069
00:50:26,440 --> 00:50:28,525
-It's okay.
-We already saw it.

1070
00:50:28,608 --> 00:50:30,152
It didn't even take nine minutes.

1071
00:50:30,235 --> 00:50:31,069
Nine minutes?

1072
00:50:31,153 --> 00:50:32,487
The time to start going down.

1073
00:50:32,571 --> 00:50:34,281
I think we were here for 10 to 15 minutes.

1074
00:50:34,364 --> 00:50:36,366
Really? You got here so fast.

1075
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:37,284
Let's descend.

1076
00:50:37,367 --> 00:50:39,161
12:40 P.M.
DESCENDING 9 MINUTES AFTER MEETING

1077
00:50:39,244 --> 00:50:40,746
-Let's go down.
-Good job.

1078
00:50:44,249 --> 00:50:48,754
LEAVING A CLEAR BAENGNOKDAM BEHIND

1079
00:50:48,837 --> 00:50:50,380
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

1080
00:50:50,464 --> 00:50:52,716
THEY GO DOWN THE SEONGPANAK TRAIL

1081
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:54,217
Hello.

1082
00:50:55,010 --> 00:50:56,011
Hello.

1083
00:50:57,053 --> 00:50:58,138
You can do it.

1084
00:51:00,432 --> 00:51:02,017
Hey, Producer Nah,

1085
00:51:02,100 --> 00:51:04,352
you automatically cheer people on
when you descend.

1086
00:51:05,061 --> 00:51:07,522
We've been up here, so it feels good.

1087
00:51:07,606 --> 00:51:09,566
-You can do it!
-Good luck!

1088
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:11,693
Good luck.

1089
00:51:11,777 --> 00:51:12,611
You can do it.

1090
00:51:12,694 --> 00:51:15,030
You become brighter
and more enthusiastic too.

1091
00:51:15,113 --> 00:51:16,615
-Right.
-"Good luck!"

1092
00:51:18,116 --> 00:51:19,201
Let's go!

1093
00:51:19,284 --> 00:51:23,288
DESCEND CLUB'S FAVORITE PART IS DESCENDING

1094
00:51:23,872 --> 00:51:27,501
DESCENDING SEONGPANAK TRAIL
ON A SMOOTH PATH OF WOODEN STAIRS

1095
00:51:28,168 --> 00:51:29,711
LAUGHING

1096
00:51:29,795 --> 00:51:30,796
What is it, Dowoon?

1097
00:51:31,546 --> 00:51:35,550
I was just thinking
how this is so different from our trail.

1098
00:51:37,969 --> 00:51:40,430
People were sledding down our trail.

1099
00:51:40,514 --> 00:51:41,556
I know, right?

1100
00:51:43,225 --> 00:51:44,810
Still, this is nice.

1101
00:51:44,893 --> 00:51:47,687
Take a good look.
This view is a really rare sight.

1102
00:51:47,771 --> 00:51:48,772
Okay.

1103
00:51:49,731 --> 00:51:51,775
I hear it's hard to see.

1104
00:51:51,858 --> 00:51:53,360
Yeah, we chose a great day.

1105
00:51:55,153 --> 00:51:56,112
This is nice.

1106
00:52:12,003 --> 00:52:17,551
DRONE FILMING WAS ALLOWED AFTER DISCUSSION
WITH HALLASAN NATIONAL PARK

1107
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:19,636
Was it around here?

1108
00:52:19,719 --> 00:52:21,888
I hiked while admiring the view here.

1109
00:52:21,972 --> 00:52:23,431
I kept taking photos too.

1110
00:52:23,515 --> 00:52:27,227
Honestly, I don't regret
hiking up here…

1111
00:52:28,311 --> 00:52:29,312
because it's beautiful.

1112
00:52:30,480 --> 00:52:32,357
I got a good night's sleep,
so it was better.

1113
00:52:32,440 --> 00:52:34,234
Yes. I feel refreshed.

1114
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:36,945
You still seem okay, Tarzzan.

1115
00:52:37,028 --> 00:52:38,405
TAKING A BREAK

1116
00:52:38,488 --> 00:52:39,948
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

1117
00:52:40,031 --> 00:52:41,825
TEARING UP

1118
00:52:41,908 --> 00:52:43,159
You seem a bit drained.

1119
00:52:43,243 --> 00:52:44,578
Yeah, I want to go home.

1120
00:52:44,661 --> 00:52:45,495
Why?

1121
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:47,539
-Sorry?
-Did you hurt your knee?

1122
00:52:48,123 --> 00:52:49,040
Am I injured?

1123
00:52:49,124 --> 00:52:50,959
-These hard trails…
-He wants to go home.

1124
00:52:51,042 --> 00:52:52,377
Hiking today made me think.

1125
00:52:52,460 --> 00:52:54,212
Please don't give us hard trails.

1126
00:52:54,796 --> 00:52:57,257
What is this? He can't even enjoy it.

1127
00:52:57,340 --> 00:52:58,967
Look at his face.

1128
00:52:59,050 --> 00:52:59,885
DEPRESSED

1129
00:52:59,968 --> 00:53:01,219
It's like you're bullying him.

1130
00:53:01,303 --> 00:53:03,013
After taking this trail, I'm certain.

1131
00:53:03,805 --> 00:53:05,473
Please don't give us hard trails.

1132
00:53:05,557 --> 00:53:07,017
No one enjoys it.

1133
00:53:07,100 --> 00:53:08,727
Seriously, I'm telling you.

1134
00:53:08,810 --> 00:53:10,186
Today's trail. What is it?

1135
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:11,146
Seong…

1136
00:53:11,229 --> 00:53:12,480
Seongchanseong?

1137
00:53:12,981 --> 00:53:14,274
LAUGHING

1138
00:53:14,357 --> 00:53:15,483
Seongpanak?

1139
00:53:15,567 --> 00:53:18,111
Seongpanak made me realize
it shouldn't be too hard.

1140
00:53:18,194 --> 00:53:19,988
THE COMPLAINER IS AS BUSY AS EVER

1141
00:53:20,071 --> 00:53:22,616
Making the show's cast suffer
is outdated now.

1142
00:53:24,159 --> 00:53:25,493
I'll drive on the way back.

1143
00:53:25,577 --> 00:53:27,037
-I'll do it.
-No.

1144
00:53:27,120 --> 00:53:28,663
We'll take care of you today.

1145
00:53:30,081 --> 00:53:31,124
BOWING

1146
00:53:31,207 --> 00:53:32,083
Seongpanak.

1147
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,710
Seongpanak sounds like

1148
00:53:33,793 --> 00:53:35,629
the name of a post
from the Joseon Dynasty.

1149
00:53:36,129 --> 00:53:37,547
-Seongpanak.
-They're the ministers.

1150
00:53:37,631 --> 00:53:39,174
We're slaves. They're the ministers.

1151
00:53:39,257 --> 00:53:40,467
We're being treated well.

1152
00:53:40,550 --> 00:53:41,384
Right?

1153
00:53:41,468 --> 00:53:43,470
-Gwaneumsa is the post.
-You're not a king now.

1154
00:53:43,553 --> 00:53:44,930
AN N-RANK GWANEUMSA

1155
00:53:45,597 --> 00:53:47,641
Let me clear the path for him.

1156
00:53:49,726 --> 00:53:50,560
I'll clear the path.

1157
00:53:50,644 --> 00:53:53,271
HERE COMES TEAM GWANEUMSA
ON THE SNOWY ROAD

1158
00:53:53,355 --> 00:53:55,106
The Honorable Gwaneumsas are on their way.

1159
00:53:56,441 --> 00:53:57,567
"The Honorable Gwaneumsas."

1160
00:53:58,568 --> 00:54:00,153
I mean, I'm so amazed

1161
00:54:00,236 --> 00:54:02,530
that Car, the garden
has so much energy left.

1162
00:54:04,991 --> 00:54:05,825
Right.

1163
00:54:05,909 --> 00:54:06,743
Excuse me.

1164
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:08,662
We didn't take a Polaroid photo.

1165
00:54:08,745 --> 00:54:09,621
Oh, right.

1166
00:54:09,704 --> 00:54:12,707
THEY FORGOT A SUMMIT PROMISE

1167
00:54:12,791 --> 00:54:14,751
-I knew I forgot something.
-Me too.

1168
00:54:14,834 --> 00:54:16,962
Let's take it at the Jindallaebat Shelter.

1169
00:54:17,045 --> 00:54:17,879
Sure.

1170
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:22,217
THEY ARRIVE AT JINDALLAEBAT SHELTER

1171
00:54:22,300 --> 00:54:23,134
Here we go.

1172
00:54:23,218 --> 00:54:25,428
A BIT LATE BUT THEY KEEP THEIR PROMISE

1173
00:54:36,356 --> 00:54:39,859
MINISTER OF TRANSPORT IS DRAINED

1174
00:54:39,943 --> 00:54:41,903
Goodness, this is nice.

1175
00:54:43,279 --> 00:54:48,034
TAKING SOLO SHOTS

1176
00:54:49,452 --> 00:54:51,204
PASSING OUT THE SOLO SHOTS

1177
00:54:51,287 --> 00:54:53,415
-Are those instant photos?
-Is this product placement?

1178
00:54:53,498 --> 00:54:54,791
No, it's just…

1179
00:54:57,293 --> 00:54:58,712
Why do you two hike?

1180
00:54:59,379 --> 00:55:00,630
SUDDENLY INTERVIEWING HIKERS

1181
00:55:00,714 --> 00:55:02,215
I get to overcome my limits.

1182
00:55:02,298 --> 00:55:03,633
-That's so cool.
-That's cool.

1183
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:06,052
We're doing this show
to get that kind of answer.

1184
00:55:06,136 --> 00:55:06,970
That's very cool.

1185
00:55:07,762 --> 00:55:08,680
Your limits?

1186
00:55:09,514 --> 00:55:11,057
-Overcoming them.
-To overcome them?

1187
00:55:12,100 --> 00:55:13,393
Which mountains have you hiked?

1188
00:55:14,019 --> 00:55:16,187
Have you been any other mountains?

1189
00:55:16,271 --> 00:55:19,315
Just Gwanaksan and Bukhansan.

1190
00:55:19,399 --> 00:55:20,316
Just the nearby ones.

1191
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:22,318
A few in Seoul and then Hallasan?

1192
00:55:22,944 --> 00:55:24,404
This is my third attempt.

1193
00:55:25,155 --> 00:55:27,282
You came to Hallasan three times,

1194
00:55:27,365 --> 00:55:29,117
-and today's the first sunny day?
-Yes.

1195
00:55:29,200 --> 00:55:31,202
You don't want to lose to yourself, right?

1196
00:55:31,286 --> 00:55:32,370
-Right.
-We've already lost.

1197
00:55:34,080 --> 00:55:35,081
Quick acceptance.

1198
00:55:35,707 --> 00:55:36,750
No, we won today.

1199
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:37,959
Let us win too.

1200
00:55:38,043 --> 00:55:39,711
We're going to lose again tomorrow.

1201
00:55:39,794 --> 00:55:41,463
-And the day after…
-What are we climbing?

1202
00:55:41,546 --> 00:55:42,922
We're just going to lose.

1203
00:55:43,882 --> 00:55:46,259
I went to your latest concert.

1204
00:55:46,342 --> 00:55:47,177
What?

1205
00:55:47,260 --> 00:55:48,219
I really enjoyed it.

1206
00:55:48,303 --> 00:55:50,764
When? First day or second day?

1207
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:52,682
-I went on Saturday.
-Saturday?

1208
00:55:52,766 --> 00:55:54,476
She's a huge fan then!

1209
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:57,687
SHE TURNS OUT TO BE
A BIG FAN OF CAR, THE GARDEN

1210
00:55:57,771 --> 00:55:59,147
Did he do a good job then?

1211
00:55:59,230 --> 00:56:00,523
He really…

1212
00:56:00,607 --> 00:56:02,025
-He touched our hearts.
-Yes.

1213
00:56:02,650 --> 00:56:04,652
GIVING HER HIS POLAROID PHOTO

1214
00:56:04,736 --> 00:56:05,570
Thank you.

1215
00:56:05,653 --> 00:56:06,488
All of a sudden?

1216
00:56:06,571 --> 00:56:07,697
It's a photo card.

1217
00:56:07,781 --> 00:56:08,615
It's his photo card?

1218
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:11,034
It really is a photo card. An instant one.

1219
00:56:11,117 --> 00:56:13,328
AN INSTANT PHOTOCARD FOR A REAL FAN

1220
00:56:13,411 --> 00:56:15,789
They're my valued customers.

1221
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:16,790
That is amazing.

1222
00:56:16,873 --> 00:56:18,083
That really is so cool.

1223
00:56:18,166 --> 00:56:21,878
You were able to overcome your own limits.

1224
00:56:21,961 --> 00:56:24,714
And she happens to be your fan.

1225
00:56:24,798 --> 00:56:26,216
THE SINGER AND FAN ARE SO DIFFERENT

1226
00:56:26,299 --> 00:56:29,427
She was a fan,
and they had come to my concert.

1227
00:56:30,095 --> 00:56:32,347
That really warmed my heart.

1228
00:56:34,057 --> 00:56:35,350
Thank you so much.

1229
00:56:37,435 --> 00:56:38,561
They're so cool.

1230
00:56:42,982 --> 00:56:44,484
I have nothing to give you but this.

1231
00:56:44,567 --> 00:56:46,194
No, you don't have to.

1232
00:56:46,277 --> 00:56:47,362
I've eaten a lot.

1233
00:56:47,445 --> 00:56:48,488
Share these with everyone.

1234
00:56:48,571 --> 00:56:49,989
Really? Thank you.

1235
00:56:52,242 --> 00:56:53,535
Let's get moving now.

1236
00:56:53,618 --> 00:56:55,578
1:50 P.M.
THEY START DESCENDING AGAIN

1237
00:56:56,371 --> 00:56:58,206
We're about a third there, right?

1238
00:56:59,332 --> 00:57:00,667
A third? Yes.

1239
00:57:01,167 --> 00:57:05,463
THE WARM AFTERNOON SUN

1240
00:57:06,631 --> 00:57:09,759
THE MELTED TRAIL ON THE DESCENT

1241
00:57:09,843 --> 00:57:13,012
"ASCENDING IS HARD,
BUT DESCENDING IS DANGEROUS"

1242
00:57:13,096 --> 00:57:14,222
REFER TO EPISODE 2

1243
00:57:14,305 --> 00:57:18,059
ENTERING THE SLIPPERY AREA

1244
00:57:18,643 --> 00:57:22,147
PRACTICALLY SLIDING DOWN

1245
00:57:24,732 --> 00:57:28,194
GWANEUMSA TEAM'S LEGS HAVE BECOME WEAK

1246
00:57:29,112 --> 00:57:32,323
THEY USE INERTIA TO DESCEND

1247
00:57:32,407 --> 00:57:34,617
WOBBLING LIKE A DASHBOARD ORNAMENT

1248
00:57:34,701 --> 00:57:36,619
LAUGHS

1249
00:57:40,415 --> 00:57:43,126
Can I take off my jacket here?

1250
00:57:43,209 --> 00:57:44,419
We'll rest and regroup here.

1251
00:57:44,502 --> 00:57:45,879
2:30 P.M.
PAUSING TO ADJUST CLOTHES

1252
00:57:45,962 --> 00:57:47,046
Sounds good.

1253
00:57:48,089 --> 00:57:48,923
-Nice.
-It's hot now.

1254
00:57:49,007 --> 00:57:50,008
Let's eat some chocolate.

1255
00:57:50,091 --> 00:57:51,217
-Sure.
-Sure.

1256
00:57:52,218 --> 00:57:53,470
SHARING CHOCOLATES FROM HIS FAN

1257
00:57:53,553 --> 00:57:55,430
-What's that?
-Chocolate.

1258
00:57:55,513 --> 00:57:56,848
-Want some?
-It's huge.

1259
00:57:57,432 --> 00:58:00,059
You've realized the importance of sugar.

1260
00:58:00,143 --> 00:58:01,728
I suddenly had a craving.

1261
00:58:05,231 --> 00:58:06,065
Dowoon.

1262
00:58:07,442 --> 00:58:09,486
YUM

1263
00:58:10,778 --> 00:58:13,865
THEY ALL STAND AS THEY REST

1264
00:58:20,371 --> 00:58:23,708
My legs stay fatigued if I don't sit down.

1265
00:58:23,791 --> 00:58:25,376
How are you guys still standing?

1266
00:58:26,878 --> 00:58:29,464
USING A FILM CAMERA

1267
00:58:30,131 --> 00:58:31,758
You look like you're on a hunger strike.

1268
00:58:31,841 --> 00:58:33,551
If we had a bamboo tree poking out…

1269
00:58:33,635 --> 00:58:35,595
I won't go.

1270
00:58:37,055 --> 00:58:38,473
Tell the supervisor to come out.

1271
00:58:39,349 --> 00:58:40,975
But he's doing that as the supervisor.

1272
00:58:41,059 --> 00:58:42,268
Right.

1273
00:58:42,352 --> 00:58:43,436
It's so discouraging.

1274
00:58:44,938 --> 00:58:46,272
He's a bit…

1275
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:53,279
He keeps saying things by himself
from the back.

1276
00:58:53,363 --> 00:58:55,657
"Hey, tell me if anyone wants to rest."

1277
00:58:55,740 --> 00:58:57,116
Then, he suddenly says, "Me."

1278
00:58:59,035 --> 00:59:01,329
"Is there anywhere I can sit?"
We just stand and rest.

1279
00:59:01,412 --> 00:59:02,622
"But I have to sit."

1280
00:59:02,705 --> 00:59:04,082
HE'S MET SOMEONE WORSE THAN HIM

1281
00:59:05,333 --> 00:59:06,167
Okay.

1282
00:59:07,919 --> 00:59:09,671
Let's hit the shelter.

1283
00:59:10,838 --> 00:59:11,673
-Sorry?
-Pardon?

1284
00:59:11,756 --> 00:59:12,757
Let's go straight there.

1285
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:15,260
Chae-min, we wasted so much time
because of you.

1286
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:17,762
SHAMELESS

1287
00:59:17,845 --> 00:59:19,389
We took a break because of him.

1288
00:59:19,472 --> 00:59:21,015
But he goes, "Let's get a move on."

1289
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:22,684
SHAMELESS SUPERVISOR

1290
00:59:22,767 --> 00:59:24,852
And his choice of words was
"hit the shelter."

1291
00:59:24,936 --> 00:59:28,273
He certainly chooses sexy words to use.

1292
00:59:29,482 --> 00:59:30,775
That annoyed me a little bit.

1293
00:59:30,858 --> 00:59:33,653
Our youngest members are struggling,
so I spoke up for them.

1294
00:59:33,736 --> 00:59:35,280
He probably can't hit it anyway.

1295
00:59:37,490 --> 00:59:38,491
"Let's hit the shelter."

1296
00:59:43,246 --> 00:59:44,455
<i>We're halfway there.</i>

1297
00:59:44,539 --> 00:59:45,873
CURRENT LOCATION

1298
00:59:45,957 --> 00:59:46,958
<i>We're exactly halfway.</i>

1299
00:59:48,459 --> 00:59:50,503
It's going to feel so good
on the way back home.

1300
00:59:51,588 --> 00:59:52,630
Inside that van.

1301
00:59:53,798 --> 00:59:56,009
Our accommodation this time
is really good.

1302
00:59:56,092 --> 00:59:56,968
Right.

1303
00:59:57,051 --> 00:59:59,345
I saw one room was empty.
Why aren't you using it?

1304
00:59:59,429 --> 01:00:02,390
Exactly. I thought Tarzzan and Chae-min
would sleep separately,

1305
01:00:02,473 --> 01:00:03,474
but they slept together.

1306
01:00:03,558 --> 01:00:04,642
We like sleeping together.

1307
01:00:06,144 --> 01:00:06,978
Right?

1308
01:00:08,938 --> 01:00:12,233
Dowoon seemed to sleep pretty comfortably.

1309
01:00:12,317 --> 01:00:13,359
I sleep really well.

1310
01:00:13,443 --> 01:00:15,028
You sleep so well on the floor.

1311
01:00:15,111 --> 01:00:17,322
The second floor room is the best one.

1312
01:00:17,405 --> 01:00:19,073
It's almost like your own private place

1313
01:00:19,157 --> 01:00:20,074
on the second floor.

1314
01:00:20,158 --> 01:00:22,076
It is, but he sleeps in a small room.

1315
01:00:22,160 --> 01:00:23,161
That's right.

1316
01:00:23,244 --> 01:00:26,414
I went to a small room,
thinking you guys would come up.

1317
01:00:26,497 --> 01:00:28,750
Each one of us…

1318
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:30,126
We sacrificed for each other.

1319
01:00:30,209 --> 01:00:33,129
We're being considerate,
but it turned out a bit strange.

1320
01:00:34,088 --> 01:00:37,342
CHAE-MIN AND TARZZAN
1ST FLOOR ROOM

1321
01:00:37,425 --> 01:00:40,553
DOWOON
1ST FLOOR LIVING ROOM

1322
01:00:40,637 --> 01:00:43,765
CAR, THE GARDEN
2ND FLOOR SMALL ROOM

1323
01:00:44,349 --> 01:00:48,436
A SAD TALE
OF HOW THE BEST ROOM WAS LEFT EMPTY

1324
01:00:49,270 --> 01:00:51,773
-The path is nice now.
-I know.

1325
01:00:52,607 --> 01:00:54,651
And a nice forest appears here.

1326
01:00:54,734 --> 01:00:56,110
Oh, here.

1327
01:00:56,653 --> 01:00:57,612
We know this place.

1328
01:00:57,695 --> 01:00:58,988
Oh, here?

1329
01:00:59,489 --> 01:01:00,531
The phytoncides.

1330
01:01:00,615 --> 01:01:01,491
Okay.

1331
01:01:01,574 --> 01:01:02,408
How did you know?

1332
01:01:02,992 --> 01:01:04,577
We passed a place like this too.

1333
01:01:05,578 --> 01:01:07,038
I thought it was only on our trail.

1334
01:01:08,665 --> 01:01:13,419
THE MEMORABLE VIEW
OF CEDAR TREES ON BOTH TRAILS

1335
01:01:21,511 --> 01:01:26,724
IT FEELS NICE THE SECOND TIME TOO

1336
01:01:33,898 --> 01:01:37,568
Do we get a certificate
with the selfie we took earlier?

1337
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:44,659
It's to prove we've been to the summit
of this mountain.

1338
01:01:45,618 --> 01:01:47,537
I see the building over there.

1339
01:01:48,162 --> 01:01:49,288
What? You're right.

1340
01:01:51,332 --> 01:01:53,835
ARRIVING WITH A GROAN TODAY TOO

1341
01:01:53,918 --> 01:01:54,919
We're here.

1342
01:01:55,962 --> 01:01:58,506
-Good job, everyone.
-Good job.

1343
01:01:58,589 --> 01:01:59,924
MOANING

1344
01:02:01,509 --> 01:02:05,680
3:55 P.M.
DESCENT COMPLETE

1345
01:02:06,973 --> 01:02:08,516
-Good job, everyone.
-Well done.

1346
01:02:08,599 --> 01:02:11,769
THE HIKE ENDS AFTER ABOUT 9 HOURS

1347
01:02:13,062 --> 01:02:14,981
GRIMACING

1348
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:18,943
SUMMIT CERTIFICATES CAN BE ISSUED
AT THE VISITOR CENTER

1349
01:02:19,026 --> 01:02:23,364
SUMMIT CERTIFICATE
AND VISITOR RESERVATION QR CODE ISSUANCE

1350
01:02:23,448 --> 01:02:25,742
1. FILL OUT FORM
ON HALLASAN NATIONAL PARK WEBSITE

1351
01:02:25,825 --> 01:02:28,327
2. ATTACH PHOTO TAKEN AT SUMMIT AND APPLY

1352
01:02:28,411 --> 01:02:30,872
3. ENTER VERIFICATION NUMBER INTO KIOSK

1353
01:02:30,955 --> 01:02:33,374
4. PRINT OUT SUMMIT CERTIFICATE

1354
01:02:33,458 --> 01:02:36,294
JEJU SPECIAL SELF-GOVERNING PROVINCE
CERTIFICATE OF HALLASAN HIKING

1355
01:02:36,377 --> 01:02:38,921
NAME: LEE CHAE-MIN
DATE: FEBRUARY 4, 2026

1356
01:02:39,005 --> 01:02:40,798
HOW DID IT FEEL TO HIKE HALLASAN?

1357
01:02:40,882 --> 01:02:41,841
<i>For the first time,</i>

1358
01:02:41,924 --> 01:02:45,970
we hiked up and down with various people.

1359
01:02:46,053 --> 01:02:49,140
We cheered each other on
and exchanged greetings.

1360
01:02:49,223 --> 01:02:51,225
When we were going up,
those coming down said,

1361
01:02:51,309 --> 01:02:53,102
"Have a good hike."

1362
01:02:53,186 --> 01:02:55,229
THEY HIKED HALLASAN
ALONGSIDE MANY OTHER HIKERS

1363
01:02:56,314 --> 01:02:58,816
It created a sort of synergy.

1364
01:02:58,900 --> 01:03:00,860
I thought,
"People in Korea are still kind."

1365
01:03:00,943 --> 01:03:05,323
I felt that and it made me happy.

1366
01:03:05,406 --> 01:03:07,784
The Hallasan hike comforted me…

1367
01:03:09,410 --> 01:03:11,120
and helped me recharge emotionally.

1368
01:03:13,164 --> 01:03:16,876
Then, out of Seoraksan,
Taebaeksan, and Hallasan,

1369
01:03:16,959 --> 01:03:18,711
which mountain did you prefer?

1370
01:03:18,795 --> 01:03:19,962
Which did I prefer?

1371
01:03:20,046 --> 01:03:22,673
I'd definitely say Hallasan.

1372
01:03:24,050 --> 01:03:25,676
The other two mountains were…

1373
01:03:27,929 --> 01:03:29,305
NOTHING BUT BITTER MEMORIES

1374
01:03:29,388 --> 01:03:32,642
If I had to choose one to visit,
I'd go to Taebaeksan.

1375
01:03:32,725 --> 01:03:34,685
Taebaeksan was really beautiful.

1376
01:03:34,769 --> 01:03:35,978
Hallasan was…

1377
01:03:36,896 --> 01:03:37,730
Well…

1378
01:03:38,231 --> 01:03:39,398
If the trail had been better,

1379
01:03:39,482 --> 01:03:43,653
it would've made for a very fond memory.

1380
01:03:44,278 --> 01:03:46,072
But it was really tough.

1381
01:03:46,155 --> 01:03:49,367
I don't think I'll even pee
in Hallasan's direction again.

1382
01:03:50,618 --> 01:03:52,954
If you were to compare
Seoraksan and Hallasan…

1383
01:03:53,037 --> 01:03:53,871
Okay.

1384
01:03:53,955 --> 01:03:56,666
Hiking to Seoraksan's Huiungak Shelter
versus hiking Hallasan.

1385
01:03:56,749 --> 01:03:57,792
That's a tough one.

1386
01:03:59,418 --> 01:04:01,671
Seoraksan was definitely tougher.

1387
01:04:02,255 --> 01:04:05,675
If Seoraksan was 100 in difficulty,
Hallasan was 80.

1388
01:04:05,758 --> 01:04:06,926
-It's 80?
-Yes, 80.

1389
01:04:07,969 --> 01:04:10,096
No, make that 90.

1390
01:04:10,179 --> 01:04:12,181
-As of now.
-Okay.

1391
01:04:13,015 --> 01:04:15,560
Could you share a good tip
or trick you might have?

1392
01:04:15,643 --> 01:04:16,602
A good tip?

1393
01:04:16,686 --> 01:04:19,730
Think of it as walking slowly.

1394
01:04:19,814 --> 01:04:21,274
And what was it?

1395
01:04:21,357 --> 01:04:23,568
Prepare your trail food well.

1396
01:04:23,651 --> 01:04:27,029
Bringing three or four bottles of water
was a perfect amount.

1397
01:04:27,113 --> 01:04:29,657
Why on earth do you think people hike?

1398
01:04:31,534 --> 01:04:32,785
Maybe it's this.

1399
01:04:32,869 --> 01:04:33,870
It's like…

1400
01:04:34,871 --> 01:04:36,330
Right, we interviewed them.

1401
01:04:36,414 --> 01:04:40,209
You know,
you want to test your own limits.

1402
01:04:40,877 --> 01:04:43,170
-The people you met while descending?
-Yes.

1403
01:04:45,006 --> 01:04:49,302
Yes, for people like her,
that would be the reason.

1404
01:04:50,136 --> 01:04:53,472
I understand people who like it.

1405
01:04:53,556 --> 01:04:56,142
But I also understand those who hate it.

1406
01:04:56,225 --> 01:04:57,810
So I'm in the middle.

1407
01:04:57,894 --> 01:05:00,271
"You could like hiking because of this."

1408
01:05:00,354 --> 01:05:01,314
But…

1409
01:05:02,690 --> 01:05:04,692
I think it has to do
with your disposition.

1410
01:05:06,694 --> 01:05:10,573
When we asked someone why they hiked,

1411
01:05:10,656 --> 01:05:15,536
they said they were doing a challenge
of hiking 100 famous mountains.

1412
01:05:15,620 --> 01:05:21,375
So I thought,
"Does Korea even have 100 mountains?"

1413
01:05:22,251 --> 01:05:23,252
How's the view up there?

1414
01:05:23,336 --> 01:05:24,170
ON SEONGPANAK TRAIL

1415
01:05:24,253 --> 01:05:26,422
You're almost there.
The view is amazing today.

1416
01:05:26,505 --> 01:05:27,632
Why do you hike?

1417
01:05:27,715 --> 01:05:28,549
Why do I hike?

1418
01:05:28,633 --> 01:05:30,509
I'm trying to hike 100 famous mountains.

1419
01:05:30,593 --> 01:05:31,969
-A challenge?
-Really?

1420
01:05:32,053 --> 01:05:33,137
How many have you hiked?

1421
01:05:33,220 --> 01:05:34,847
We've done about 30.

1422
01:05:36,933 --> 01:05:38,392
Have you been to Seoraksan too?

1423
01:05:38,476 --> 01:05:40,144
-Not yet but--
-Don't go.

1424
01:05:40,227 --> 01:05:41,562
Our first mountain was Seoraksan.

1425
01:05:41,646 --> 01:05:43,189
THE HIKERS LAUGH

1426
01:05:44,023 --> 01:05:46,525
I really respect them.

1427
01:05:47,610 --> 01:05:51,238
But just before we started this interview,

1428
01:05:51,322 --> 01:05:54,075
I put the badge I received yesterday
on my bag.

1429
01:05:54,158 --> 01:05:56,077
<i>They're like tokens of achievement</i>
<i>on my bag…</i>

1430
01:05:56,702 --> 01:05:59,664
<i>and I'm starting to have fun</i>
<i>collecting them.</i>

1431
01:05:59,747 --> 01:06:01,374
SEORAKSAN, TAEBAEKSAN

1432
01:06:02,124 --> 01:06:03,501
To be honest…

1433
01:06:05,044 --> 01:06:06,379
I like being active.

1434
01:06:07,546 --> 01:06:10,174
I just play along
and pretend to not like it for the show.

1435
01:06:10,967 --> 01:06:12,593
I actually think it's not that bad.

1436
01:06:12,677 --> 01:06:13,719
You can like it.

1437
01:06:13,803 --> 01:06:14,887
Right.

1438
01:06:14,971 --> 01:06:16,389
I think it's not bad.

1439
01:06:17,139 --> 01:06:19,892
I like to exercise, so it's kind of fun.

1440
01:06:19,976 --> 01:06:21,686
I like looking at the scenery too.

1441
01:06:22,478 --> 01:06:25,982
Yes, I think hiking is fun.

1442
01:06:29,318 --> 01:06:32,446
While interviewing other people,

1443
01:06:32,530 --> 01:06:35,908
I thought, "I could agree with that."

1444
01:06:35,992 --> 01:06:36,826
It's a bit like…

1445
01:06:38,953 --> 01:06:40,371
"I want to make myself suffer.

1446
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:45,126
I want to punish myself."

1447
01:06:46,502 --> 01:06:48,838
Perhaps those are the types of people
who hike.

1448
01:06:48,921 --> 01:06:50,589
"I'm on a diet, but I ate too much."

1449
01:06:50,673 --> 01:06:53,426
Or, "I should've done my homework today,
but I didn't."

1450
01:06:54,135 --> 01:06:56,012
"Then, I have to go up the mountain."

1451
01:06:57,847 --> 01:07:01,225
The middle schooler
and high schooler didn't say it,

1452
01:07:01,308 --> 01:07:03,310
but their parents
could've been punishing them.

1453
01:07:07,523 --> 01:07:09,108
BAENGNOKDAM, HALLASAN

1454
01:07:16,574 --> 01:07:17,408
<i>Damijin.</i>

1455
01:07:17,491 --> 01:07:18,993
TARZZAN'S FIRST MEAL AFTER DESCENT

1456
01:07:19,076 --> 01:07:20,161
They have yellowtail.

1457
01:07:20,244 --> 01:07:21,996
A RESTAURANT SERVING FRESH, RAW WILD FISH

1458
01:07:24,248 --> 01:07:26,292
A VARIETY OF GLISTENING RAW FISH

1459
01:07:26,876 --> 01:07:30,713
AND SPICY FISH STEW TO REFRESH THE PALATE

1460
01:07:30,796 --> 01:07:33,340
PLUS A VARIETY OF SIDE DISHES

1461
01:07:33,424 --> 01:07:36,135
IT'S READY FOR DESCEND CLUB TO EAT
AFTER THEIR EFFORTS

1462
01:07:36,218 --> 01:07:37,261
Gosh.

1463
01:07:38,971 --> 01:07:40,806
SIGHING

1464
01:07:40,890 --> 01:07:42,224
WINCING

1465
01:07:42,308 --> 01:07:44,935
EVERYONE GROANS AS THEY SIT DOWN

1466
01:07:45,019 --> 01:07:47,271
BUT ONE SEAT IS EMPTY

1467
01:07:47,354 --> 01:07:48,564
Why isn't Dowoon coming?

1468
01:07:54,737 --> 01:07:56,489
Three spans? 23?

1469
01:07:56,572 --> 01:07:57,865
Sixty-and-a-half.

1470
01:07:58,365 --> 01:07:59,992
FISHING FANATIC IS BUSY MEASURING SIZES

1471
01:08:00,076 --> 01:08:01,660
It must be around 75 cm.

1472
01:08:02,328 --> 01:08:04,580
-This is crazy.
-This is awesome.

1473
01:08:05,372 --> 01:08:07,333
-Let's eat now.
-Okay.

1474
01:08:07,416 --> 01:08:09,543
NO TIME TO WAIT

1475
01:08:09,627 --> 01:08:10,920
Let give it a taste.

1476
01:08:11,003 --> 01:08:12,421
Enjoy your food.

1477
01:08:18,719 --> 01:08:20,638
IT MAKES HIM SMILE

1478
01:08:22,973 --> 01:08:23,974
YUM

1479
01:08:24,975 --> 01:08:27,228
TAKES A BITE OF BOILED PORK SIDE DISH

1480
01:08:31,273 --> 01:08:34,443
DOWOON JOINS AND WORKS UP HIS APPETITE
WITH CRISPY FRIED FOOD

1481
01:08:35,152 --> 01:08:37,905
DIPS RAW FISH RIGHT INTO CHOJANG
AND TAKES A BITE

1482
01:08:37,988 --> 01:08:38,823
YUM

1483
01:08:39,907 --> 01:08:41,617
-This is good.
-It's good?

1484
01:08:49,708 --> 01:08:51,502
This restaurant is good.

1485
01:08:51,585 --> 01:08:52,628
Is it good?

1486
01:08:52,711 --> 01:08:53,546
Yeah.

1487
01:08:53,629 --> 01:08:55,047
You're good at finding restaurants.

1488
01:08:55,131 --> 01:08:56,924
VERY SATISFIED WITH TARZZAN'S CHOICES

1489
01:08:57,508 --> 01:08:58,467
What's this?

1490
01:09:00,386 --> 01:09:01,595
It's largescale blackfish.

1491
01:09:01,679 --> 01:09:02,721
-What?
-Blackfish?

1492
01:09:02,805 --> 01:09:03,681
Yeah, it's expensive.

1493
01:09:04,306 --> 01:09:05,599
Can you tell just from looking?

1494
01:09:06,142 --> 01:09:08,394
Of course. Try pointing to one.

1495
01:09:08,477 --> 01:09:10,604
A GAME OF "GUESS THE FISH" SUDDENLY STARTS

1496
01:09:10,688 --> 01:09:12,189
This? Convict grouper.

1497
01:09:12,273 --> 01:09:13,732
-This one.
-That's yellowtail.

1498
01:09:13,816 --> 01:09:15,401
This one.

1499
01:09:16,026 --> 01:09:17,486
That one doesn't have a name tag.

1500
01:09:17,570 --> 01:09:18,612
He was just reading these.

1501
01:09:18,696 --> 01:09:21,782
NAMES OF THE FISH
ARE WRITTEN ON THE PLATES

1502
01:09:21,866 --> 01:09:23,159
I couldn't see from here.

1503
01:09:23,242 --> 01:09:24,577
I thought so.

1504
01:09:24,660 --> 01:09:25,494
LARGESCALE BLACKFISH

1505
01:09:25,578 --> 01:09:27,371
HE TOTALLY FELL FOR IT

1506
01:09:27,454 --> 01:09:29,790
I'll let the spicy fish stew
boil down a bit more.

1507
01:09:29,874 --> 01:09:31,750
BOILED DOWN SPICY FISH STEW FOR THE END

1508
01:09:31,834 --> 01:09:33,419
Do you think they have ramyeon noodles?

1509
01:09:33,502 --> 01:09:34,336
They do.

1510
01:09:34,420 --> 01:09:35,337
-They do?
-Yes.

1511
01:09:35,421 --> 01:09:36,922
Do you want some ramyeon noodles?

1512
01:09:37,798 --> 01:09:40,843
PUTS THEM IN IMMEDIATELY

1513
01:09:40,926 --> 01:09:44,930
PUSHES THE RAMYEON IN

1514
01:09:49,602 --> 01:09:51,103
-I think it's cooked.
-It's cooked.

1515
01:09:51,187 --> 01:09:53,147
-Let's eat.
-Yeah, let's eat.

1516
01:09:54,231 --> 01:09:55,107
Help yourselves.

1517
01:09:58,277 --> 01:09:59,862
INHALING WHILE STILL STANDING

1518
01:09:59,945 --> 01:10:00,863
YUM

1519
01:10:00,946 --> 01:10:02,031
-Is it good?
-Yeah.

1520
01:10:02,990 --> 01:10:05,743
It definitely tastes better
with ramyeon noodles.

1521
01:10:06,410 --> 01:10:09,038
I've been observing you since Seoraksan.

1522
01:10:09,121 --> 01:10:11,290
You have legit ramyeon cooking skills.

1523
01:10:11,916 --> 01:10:13,542
From the way you stuff the noodles in.

1524
01:10:14,960 --> 01:10:16,045
-Really?
-Yeah.

1525
01:10:16,128 --> 01:10:18,464
BECOMES THE OFFICIAL RAMYEON MAKER
OF TAKE A HIKE!

1526
01:10:22,426 --> 01:10:24,136
BEEF BONE SOUP, JJAJANG, AND RAMYEON

1527
01:10:24,220 --> 01:10:25,638
THIS IS THEIR FOURTH RAMYEON TODAY

1528
01:10:27,973 --> 01:10:30,768
BUT THEY ALWAYS EAT
LIKE IT'S THE FIRST TIME

1529
01:10:37,274 --> 01:10:38,442
I'm so happy.

1530
01:10:39,610 --> 01:10:41,737
I feel better with some carbs in me now.

1531
01:10:42,696 --> 01:10:44,740
I'm so worried about the next mountain.

1532
01:10:45,407 --> 01:10:46,450
HOLLOW LAUGH

1533
01:10:46,533 --> 01:10:48,494
PRETENDING THEY DIDN'T HEAR HIM

1534
01:10:48,577 --> 01:10:49,745
Congratulations.

1535
01:10:49,828 --> 01:10:50,788
Your badges are here.

1536
01:10:50,871 --> 01:10:52,790
TRYING TO CHANGE THE SUBJECT TO HALLASAN

1537
01:10:52,873 --> 01:10:54,416
The badge says Baengnokdam, Hallasan.

1538
01:10:54,500 --> 01:10:56,585
BAENGNOKDAM, HALLASAN

1539
01:10:57,378 --> 01:10:58,879
This company…

1540
01:10:58,963 --> 01:10:59,797
Yes?

1541
01:10:59,880 --> 01:11:03,092
They make us clothes and badges too.

1542
01:11:03,175 --> 01:11:04,426
VERY HONORED

1543
01:11:04,510 --> 01:11:08,681
And here's the badge
for the Seongpanak team.

1544
01:11:09,515 --> 01:11:13,894
SEONGPANAK TEAM
19 KM

1545
01:11:14,603 --> 01:11:19,650
GWANEUMSA TEAM
18 KM

1546
01:11:19,733 --> 01:11:23,028
SEONGPANAK, 19 KM
GWANEUMSA, 18 KM

1547
01:11:23,779 --> 01:11:26,532
We went one kilometer further.

1548
01:11:27,157 --> 01:11:28,951
IN DISBELIEF

1549
01:11:29,034 --> 01:11:30,911
After going through all that hardship…

1550
01:11:30,995 --> 01:11:32,663
We went one kilometer longer.

1551
01:11:32,746 --> 01:11:35,207
This is really making me mad.

1552
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:37,167
FEELING CHEATED OF 1 KM

1553
01:11:38,127 --> 01:11:38,961
Ma'am.

1554
01:11:39,837 --> 01:11:40,921
-Ma'am.
-Yes?

1555
01:11:41,422 --> 01:11:42,548
Would you like a badge?

1556
01:11:43,632 --> 01:11:45,175
Do you need a badge?

1557
01:11:45,259 --> 01:11:46,760
FREE BADGE GIVEAWAY

1558
01:11:46,844 --> 01:11:48,595
Excuse me. You can't resell it.

1559
01:11:48,679 --> 01:11:50,055
-The Baengnokdam badge.
-Thank you.

1560
01:11:50,139 --> 01:11:50,973
WHAT A SHAME

1561
01:11:51,598 --> 01:11:54,351
Okay, we'll reveal the next mountain.

1562
01:11:54,435 --> 01:11:56,437
-Then, shall we wrap for today?
-Okay.

1563
01:11:56,520 --> 01:11:58,355
Gosh, the next mountain.

1564
01:12:02,318 --> 01:12:03,819
For the next quest…

1565
01:12:05,821 --> 01:12:07,364
we're going to Ulsan.

1566
01:12:07,448 --> 01:12:08,490
-Hey!
-My home?

1567
01:12:08,574 --> 01:12:09,450
It's Tarzzan's home.

1568
01:12:09,533 --> 01:12:12,870
In Tarzzan's hometown,
it's the Yeongnam Alps'

1569
01:12:12,953 --> 01:12:14,830
three-peak challenge.

1570
01:12:15,748 --> 01:12:16,749
Congratulations.

1571
01:12:18,167 --> 01:12:20,044
What are the Yeongnam Alps?

1572
01:12:20,919 --> 01:12:22,629
HE ALSO HAS NO CLUE

1573
01:12:22,713 --> 01:12:24,590
What are the Yeongnam Alps?

1574
01:12:24,673 --> 01:12:26,008
What's that?

1575
01:12:27,634 --> 01:12:30,929
YEONGNAM ALPS

1576
01:12:37,227 --> 01:12:44,193
THEY ARE THE NINE MOUNTAINS
CLUSTERED IN THE YEONGNAM REGION

1577
01:12:53,952 --> 01:12:56,163
AN ELEGANT RIDGE CONNECTING NINE PEAKS

1578
01:12:56,246 --> 01:12:58,957
THE SIGHT IS COMPARABLE TO THE ALPS,

1579
01:12:59,041 --> 01:13:04,505
SO THEY'RE NAMED THE YEONGNAM ALPS

1580
01:13:04,588 --> 01:13:07,049
THANKS TO BEING 1,000M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

1581
01:13:07,132 --> 01:13:09,927
THERE'S A PICTURESQUE VIEW
IN EVERY DIRECTION

1582
01:13:10,010 --> 01:13:15,724
THE ENDLESS EXPANSE
OF THE GOLDEN EULALIA GRASS FIELDS

1583
01:13:16,350 --> 01:13:18,560
IS THE MOST BEAUTIFUL PART
OF THE YEONGNAM ALPS

1584
01:13:19,603 --> 01:13:26,360
PEOPLE CONTINUE TO VISIT
TO TRAVERSE THE MOUNTAINS

1585
01:13:26,944 --> 01:13:30,030
AMONG THEM, DESCEND CLUB WILL HIKE

1586
01:13:30,114 --> 01:13:35,619
GANWOLSAN

1587
01:13:35,702 --> 01:13:41,250
SINBULSAN

1588
01:13:41,333 --> 01:13:46,713
YEONGCHUKSAN

1589
01:13:46,797 --> 01:13:51,218
DESCEND CLUB'S THIRD QUEST
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE

1590
01:13:51,301 --> 01:13:53,971
Hold on, that means we need to hike three.

1591
01:13:54,054 --> 01:13:56,723
It's up and down, up and down,
and up and down, right?

1592
01:13:56,807 --> 01:13:59,059
Chae-min, since when did you become
this rebellious?

1593
01:13:59,143 --> 01:14:00,310
The more you hang with them…

1594
01:14:00,394 --> 01:14:01,979
THE MEMBERS START RESEMBLING EACH OTHER

1595
01:14:02,688 --> 01:14:04,189
Jung-won, he said three peaks.

1596
01:14:04,273 --> 01:14:05,816
I'm asking ChatGPT.

1597
01:14:05,899 --> 01:14:06,900
I asked ChatGPT,

1598
01:14:06,984 --> 01:14:10,362
"Nah Yung-suk wants us to do
the Yeongnam Alps' three-peak challenge."

1599
01:14:10,446 --> 01:14:12,739
ASKING CHATGPT FOR ADVICE AGAIN

1600
01:14:12,823 --> 01:14:14,825
"Nah Yung-suk said that?

1601
01:14:16,118 --> 01:14:18,328
To be honest,
Nah Yung-suk wants you to do it

1602
01:14:18,412 --> 01:14:19,997
for just one reason.

1603
01:14:20,080 --> 01:14:22,040
He wants to bring out your true nature."

1604
01:14:22,124 --> 01:14:24,168
CHATGPT'S ANALYSIS IS FRIGHTENINGLY KEEN

1605
01:14:24,251 --> 01:14:27,588
"It's great content for the show,
but it's punishing for you."

1606
01:14:27,671 --> 01:14:29,756
You won't need to keep going
up and down mountains.

1607
01:14:29,840 --> 01:14:30,924
SEARCHING AND NOT LISTENING

1608
01:14:31,008 --> 01:14:33,010
Seven of the mountains are all connected.

1609
01:14:33,093 --> 01:14:34,678
How long will the entire trip take?

1610
01:14:34,761 --> 01:14:36,722
The whole trip will take
about eight hours.

1611
01:14:38,891 --> 01:14:39,892
SIGHING

1612
01:14:41,351 --> 01:14:43,937
THE GWANEUMSA TEAM SIGHS SIMULTANEOUSLY

1613
01:14:44,021 --> 01:14:46,148
Well, duration-wise,
it's similar to this one.

1614
01:14:46,231 --> 01:14:47,149
Yes.

1615
01:14:47,232 --> 01:14:48,525
Hey.

1616
01:14:48,609 --> 01:14:49,902
This is going to be tough.

1617
01:14:49,985 --> 01:14:52,696
ONE SEONGPANAK TEAM MEMBER
IS VERY ANGRY

1618
01:14:52,779 --> 01:14:54,990
There's no place to rest at all?

1619
01:14:55,073 --> 01:14:57,910
No, there are a lot
of well-managed resting areas.

1620
01:14:57,993 --> 01:15:00,120
It says your thighs
will get wrecked from the start.

1621
01:15:01,371 --> 01:15:04,958
"That's why Nah Yung-suk chose this.
The trail will show your true nature."

1622
01:15:05,042 --> 01:15:06,960
Then, it added a demon emoji next to it.

1623
01:15:08,378 --> 01:15:10,380
See? ChatGPT is accurate.

1624
01:15:10,464 --> 01:15:12,216
CONSULTANT'S CONCLUSION:
DEMONIC DIFFICULTY

1625
01:15:12,299 --> 01:15:15,344
I should ask my mom,
"Mom, where are the Yeongnam Alps?"

1626
01:15:15,427 --> 01:15:16,929
Call her now.

1627
01:15:18,138 --> 01:15:23,435
THIS TIME, THEY CALL TARZZAN'S MOTHER
IN ULSAN FOR ADVICE

1628
01:15:23,519 --> 01:15:25,604
<i>-Hello?</i>
-Hello?

1629
01:15:25,687 --> 01:15:26,522
<i>Hey.</i>

1630
01:15:26,605 --> 01:15:28,106
-Mom.
<i>-Yeah?</i>

1631
01:15:28,190 --> 01:15:30,567
Do you know where the Yeongnam Alps are?

1632
01:15:30,651 --> 01:15:32,069
<i>Of course, I do.</i>

1633
01:15:32,903 --> 01:15:35,030
<i>It's near Ulsan, toward Eonyang.</i>

1634
01:15:35,113 --> 01:15:38,200
<i>We went there once when you were young.</i>

1635
01:15:38,283 --> 01:15:41,328
<i>Back then…</i>

1636
01:15:41,411 --> 01:15:42,788
Did we take the car up?

1637
01:15:42,871 --> 01:15:44,081
<i>No.</i>

1638
01:15:44,164 --> 01:15:45,249
Did we walk up?

1639
01:15:45,332 --> 01:15:46,208
<i>Of course, we walked.</i>

1640
01:15:46,291 --> 01:15:48,335
Did I find it easy to hike?

1641
01:15:48,418 --> 01:15:52,130
<i>That was the only time you went hiking.</i>

1642
01:15:52,214 --> 01:15:53,382
Okay.

1643
01:15:53,465 --> 01:15:54,591
<i>You had a really hard time.</i>

1644
01:15:56,176 --> 01:15:57,219
Put me on the phone.

1645
01:15:57,761 --> 01:16:01,598
Hold on, Mom.
Car, the garden wants to speak with you.

1646
01:16:01,682 --> 01:16:03,350
-Hello, ma'am.
<i>-Hi!</i>

1647
01:16:03,433 --> 01:16:05,394
-I'd like to ask something.
<i>-Sure.</i>

1648
01:16:05,477 --> 01:16:07,145
You know Producer Nah, right?

1649
01:16:07,229 --> 01:16:08,063
<i>Yes.</i>

1650
01:16:08,146 --> 01:16:09,690
Please report him to the police.

1651
01:16:10,440 --> 01:16:14,319
-He just deceived us.
<i>-Right.</i>

1652
01:16:14,403 --> 01:16:15,571
And he's making us go hiking.

1653
01:16:15,654 --> 01:16:18,323
Your son's skin is all red now.

1654
01:16:18,407 --> 01:16:19,241
It's a mess.

1655
01:16:19,324 --> 01:16:21,159
He's completely sunburnt.

1656
01:16:21,243 --> 01:16:24,580
They're taking us to the Yeongnam Alps.

1657
01:16:24,663 --> 01:16:25,914
-But--
<i>-It's so nice there,</i>

1658
01:16:25,998 --> 01:16:28,333
<i>but now's not the right season to go.</i>

1659
01:16:28,417 --> 01:16:29,960
CLENCHING HIS EYES SHUT

1660
01:16:30,043 --> 01:16:32,170
THE EXACT OPPOSITE OF CHATGPT'S ADVICE

1661
01:16:32,254 --> 01:16:35,549
We'll come pay a visit
to say hello to you.

1662
01:16:35,632 --> 01:16:36,883
ENDING THE CALL POLITELY

1663
01:16:36,967 --> 01:16:38,510
I'll put Tarzzan back on the phone.

1664
01:16:38,594 --> 01:16:39,428
<i>Okay.</i>

1665
01:16:40,304 --> 01:16:42,889
-She sounds so young.
-Mom, I love you. Bye.

1666
01:16:42,973 --> 01:16:44,933
<i>-Okay, I love you.</i>
-Me too. Bye.

1667
01:16:45,017 --> 01:16:46,518
She's so lovely.

1668
01:16:46,602 --> 01:16:48,770
MOTHER AND SON ARE VERY AFFECTIONATE

1669
01:16:48,854 --> 01:16:52,024
She said Tarzzan hiked them with a smile
when he was in fourth grade.

1670
01:16:52,107 --> 01:16:55,319
The term "three-peak" sounds so brutal.

1671
01:16:55,902 --> 01:16:57,613
-Exactly.
-Three peaks.

1672
01:16:59,323 --> 01:17:00,741
LAUGHING

1673
01:17:00,824 --> 01:17:02,200
COMPLETELY LOSING IT

1674
01:17:02,909 --> 01:17:04,870
Hey, I'm too stressed out now.

1675
01:17:04,953 --> 01:17:06,204
Let's go eat something sweet.

1676
01:17:06,288 --> 01:17:08,832
HE NEEDS IMMEDIATE SUGAR INTAKE

1677
01:17:08,915 --> 01:17:10,792
I'm too stressed to…

1678
01:17:10,876 --> 01:17:13,503
A HARD DAY BOTH MENTALLY AND PHYSICALLY

1679
01:18:11,561 --> 01:18:13,563
Subtitle translation by: Kim Yeeun
